    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102001": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Athletic Certification Manager Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Athletic Certification Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Athletic Certification Manager Department Office of the University Registrar-0961 Requisition Number S_260530 Posting Open Date 07/16/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 07/30/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Responsible for reviewing academic records of student-athletes and documenting compliance with progress-toward-degree and other NCAA , Big Ten, and institutional academic eligibility rules in support of the Assistant Registrar and overall eligibility certification process. Remains familiar with curricular requirements across the University’s Colleges and uses Degree Audit and other reporting software to maintain NCAA eligibility database and projections of future eligibility considerations. Supports Husker Academics counseling staff and frequently handles individual questions from counselors to ensure both UNL degree progress and satisfaction of NCAA and Big Ten academic eligibility requirements for student-athletes. Generates, evaluates, and distributes daily enrollment reporting for academic status and enrollment changes. Serves as a member of AEC (Academics, Eligibility, Compliance) Committee alongside Athletics staff. Act on behalf of Assistant Registrar of Athletic Certification in cases of absence, while maintaining absolute confidentiality with highly sensitive student-athlete information. Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus 2 years of experience working in academic administration, student affairs, enrollment management, academic advising, or organizational administration required; equivalent education/experience considered. Previous employment experience working with academic program requirements Ability to analyze information obtained from reports, student systems, and statistics Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to create clear and precise documentation required. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree Previous employment experience at an NCAA member institution, with eligibility certification and/or advising Strong analytical thinking to assess situations Ability to self-manage Excellent time management with ability to prioritize tasks and projects Experience with analytical tools. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $52,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sandy Airan, sairan2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
