    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101445": {
      "title": "Assistant Paralegal (2 positions available)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Paralegal (2 positions available) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Paralegal (2 positions available) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on the words “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach you current resume as an MS Word or PDF document. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant Paralegal (2 positions available) Department College of Law-0899 Requisition Number S_260589 Posting Open Date 07/27/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Assistant Paralegal in the Clinical Law Programs ( CLP ) at the University of Nebraska College of Law. Performs primarily paralegal duties in a law office and clinical teaching environment in support of one or more in-house clinics, which may include the Debtor Defense Clinic, Estate Planning Clinic, First Amendment Clinic, Housing Justice Clinic, Nebraska Innocence Clinic, and Weibling Entrepreneurship Clinic. Provides case support, legal clerical support, administrative support related to clinical operations, and assistance to clinical faculty and student attorneys. Works closely with supervising attorneys, students, clients, courts, agencies, and community partners while maintaining strict confidentiality and supporting the educational mission of the Clinical Law Programs. About Us At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Ample paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Employee & dependent scholarship program to pursue higher education Generous retirement plans with university match Learn more about working for UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree plus three years of professional office/secretarial experience. Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Demonstrated competency in email, word processing, spreadsheets, and presentation software programs. Experience must demonstrate excellent organizational, detail orientation, proofreading, editing, grammar, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to take initiative, work under minimal supervision, and learn new software programs. Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate will have Legal clerical training. State and federal court litigation experience is desired. At least two years’ professional experience in the legal field is highly desired. Working knowledge of clerical and receptionist duties in a law office setting. Basic level knowledge of creative software such as Adobe with experience creating fillable forms and converting documents to pdf. Basic level knowledge of software programs used in the Clinics in various substantive areas of law (i.e. LawSoft or comparable child support calculations software, bankruptcy (Top Form), and legal search engines (Lexis and Westlaw). Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $24.038/hr minimum How to Apply Click on the words “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach you current resume as an MS Word or PDF document. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Kelsey Van Patten kvanpatten@unl.edu 402-472-1695 Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your professional office/secretarial experience, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your competency in email, word processing, spreadsheets, and presentation software programs. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your organizational, detail orientation, proofreading, editing, grammar, communication, and interpersonal skills. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101951": {
      "title": "IT Support Associate",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | IT Support Associate Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help IT Support Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The search committee will begin formal review of applications on September 8, 2026 and will continue until an appointment is made. Interested applicants must first go to https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101937 , click “Apply for this job,” complete the information form, and submit the following: · Letter of application addressing qualifications specific to this job description. · Names and contact information of at least three (3) professional references. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title IT Support Associate Department Hixson Lied Fine & Performing Arts-0898 Requisition Number S_260685 Posting Open Date 08/21/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/08/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The IT Support Associate provides responsive, customer-focused technology support for faculty, staff, and students across the Hixson-Lied College of Fine and Performing Arts. This position coordinates day-to-day help desk operations and works collaboratively with college and NU Information Technology Services partners to ensure reliable technology services and support. Responsibilities Include: Providing end-user, classroom, and help desk support, including troubleshooting and resolving routine and intermediate technology issues. Coordinating help desk operations by triaging support requests, escalating complex issues as appropriate, and ensuring timely follow-up and resolution. Supervising 2–3 student workers, including hiring, training, scheduling, assigning work, and ensuring consistent help desk coverage and service quality. Supporting a variety of college and NU Information Technology Services systems and services through cross-training and collaboration with technology partners. Identifying opportunities to improve technology support by analyzing service trends, researching solutions, documenting procedures, and implementing approved improvements. We Seek: A service-oriented technology professional who enjoys solving problems and helping others. The successful candidate is an effective communicator who is organized, dependable, and able to balance hands-on technical support with coordinating help desk operations and supervising student employees. Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in computer science, information technology, or a related field, plus two (2) years of progressively responsible experience providing IT, help desk, classroom technology, or related technical support. Equivalent education/experience considered. Experience troubleshooting computer hardware, software, operating systems, peripheral devices, and routine technology problems. Ability to communicate technical information to users with varying levels of technical knowledge. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Bachelor’s degree in computer science, information technology, management information systems, education technology, business, a field of the arts, or a related field. Experience supervising, training, scheduling, or providing day-to-day direction to students or other staff. Experience using help desk/ticketing, asset management, endpoint support, classroom technology, or university technology systems. Experience supporting both Mac and Windows environments. Experience assisting with technology purchasing, inventory, deployment, documentation, or service improvement. Relevant technology support certification, such as Apple, Microsoft, CompTIA, or ITIL Foundation. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $24.77/hr minimum How to Apply The search committee will begin formal review of applications on September 8, 2026 and will continue until an appointment is made. Interested applicants must first go to https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101937 , click “Apply for this job,” complete the information form, and submit the following: · Letter of application addressing qualifications specific to this job description. · Names and contact information of at least three (3) professional references. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Drew Davis drew.davis@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102172": {
      "title": "Outreach Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Outreach Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Outreach Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Outreach Specialist Department TRIO Programs-0962 Requisition Number S_260724 Posting Open Date 09/03/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/21/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Are you passionate about making sure first-generation and income-eligible scholars know that a program built for them exists? Join our team as our Outreach Specialist and be the reason they find us. As the Outreach Specialist , you will: Serve as the spokesperson for ETS (Educational Talent Search) in the community. Build strong relationships with middle school and high school Counselors, teachers, and staff that will assist with identifying eligible students. Meet with prospective students and families, answer questions and assist with the application process. Conduct parent and community outreach, including information sessions and presentations. Maintain accurate recordkeeping of recruitment efforts and progress toward enrollment objectives. Regular travel across all five service areas is required, with intensified recruitment cycles in September–October and March–April. About Us: Educational Talent Search ( ETS ) engages, empowers and supports future first generation college and under-served scholars who have the desire and potential to pursue an education beyond high school. We provide access to academic, social, and financial resources to students across five Nebraska service areas — the Lincoln Metro area and regional extension services in Schuyler, Hastings, Grand Island, and Winnebago. At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum of one (1) year of experience working with youth in an educational, social-services, or community-based setting, with demonstrated experience in outreach, recruitment, or program promotion. A valid driver’s license and ability to travel across the project’s service areas. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related discipline Bilingual proficiency (Spanish/English) Previous TRIO or pre-college access program experience. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $45,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jamil Funnah jfunnah2@unl.edu 402-472-8887 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Some evenings and weekends Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102099": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Academic Pathway Advisor (Grand Island) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Academic Pathway Advisor (Grand Island) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Academic Pathway Advisor (Grand Island) Department TRIO Programs-0962 Requisition Number S_260711 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/17/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Are you passionate about empowering first-generation and low-income students to reach their full potential? Join our team as an Academic Pathway Advisor and be a driving force in shaping brighter futures for youth in Nebraska. As the Academic Pathway Advisor , you will: Recruit, advise, and support students in the program and monitor their success. Build relationships with school counselors, families and community partners within the Grand Island/Winnebago service area Host interactive workshops, provide one-on-one advising, tutoring, and facilitate enrichment programs. Assist int the planning and execution of the summer program. This is a regionally based role for someone who thrives on autonomy. Working from a Grand Island office. Regular travel within the service area and periodic travel to Lincoln is required. About Us: Educational Talent Search ( ETS ) engages, empowers and supports potential first generation college and under-served scholars who have the desire and potential to pursue an education beyond high school. We provide access to academic, social, and financial resources to students across five Nebraska Service Areas. This position anchors our Grand Island and Winnebago service area, serving students in partnership with local school districts and the Nebraska College Preparatory Academy ( NCPA ). When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in education or a related field. Two years of experience working in an academic and/or social setting with low-income students. Demonstrated experience designing curriculum and/or workshops students. Ability to develop educational programming related to career exploration, financial literacy, and post-secondary preparation. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet the University driver eligibility requirements. (Ability to drive the University 12 passenger vans) Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in education, psychology/counseling, or a related field. Previous TRIO experience. Experience in an educational setting with middle-school and/or high school students. Demonstrated experience with managing and maintaining student records. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with families and educators—including but not limited to parents, community and school leaders, and alumni. Competent with Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, and other instructional software. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $45,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Zach Short zshort2@unl.edu 402-480-4014 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Evening and weekends as needed. Work Location (City, State) Grand Island, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
