    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101456": {
      "title": "Ag Research Technician I",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Ag Research Technician I - (Temporary Part-Time) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Ag Research Technician I - (Temporary Part-Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Ag Research Technician I - (Temporary Part-Time) Department Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center-0942 Requisition Number S_260587 Posting Open Date 07/27/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work At the UNL Pandhandle Research, Extension and Education Center in Scottsbluff, NE we innovate and conduct research to make life better for Nebraska ag producers and rural communities. As a Part-Time, Temporary Ag Research Technician I, you will: Assist with research activities in the Entomology lab at UNL’s Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center ( PREEC ), which includes but is not limited to collecting samples in the field, counting insects under a microscope, processing plant and insect samples in the lab, maintaining field trials, and housekeeping tasks such as cleaning lab supplies in the lab. This position will be under the supervision of Dr. Pin-Chu Lai, assistant professor and extension entomologist at PREEC , while working with research technician and graduate students on multiple research project. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50 FTE ) or greater. Those appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits. Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency plus one year of related experience Ability to follow instructions and protocols for research activities Ability to learn specific skills to process plant and insect samples, such as dissecting plant tissues and insect identification Ability to work in a team setting and independently while assigned to specific tasks Good communication skills and work ethics Understand the importance of research integrity Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Interest in entomology, crop protection, and ag research Experience in biological science activities Valid driver’s license and meet UNL driver’s eligibility requirements Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Danna Walker, danna.walker@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Part-Time Temporary Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Scottsbluff, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience working with insects, plants, agriculture, lab research, or related work.  Include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101971": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (Flexible Day Shift) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (Flexible Day Shift) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (Flexible Day Shift) Department Housing Facilities Custodial-11051 Requisition Number S_260631 Posting Open Date 08/11/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/08/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings. In this role you will: Perform routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities Maintain offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers Ensure a clean, safe environment for all guests Clean hard floors and carpets Mix cleaning solutions as directed Assist with event setup and conference operations as needed The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications. Depending upon level assigned, this position may: Train and oversee work of others Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment Order supplies When hired as a Hospitality Services Attendant , the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development. When hired as a Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level. Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications 8th grade education or equivalency. Ability to follow written and oral instructions. Must have the ability to understand cleaning chemicals and their application and dilution ratios. Must have the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be available via cell phone during working hours. Must be able to lift 35 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Previous custodial experience preferred. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $16.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sharleen Roth sroth6@nebraska.edu 4024723699 Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
