    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101889": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | News and Public Relations Writer/Editor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help News and Public Relations Writer/Editor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Please attach 3-5 examples of authored stories or a link as one document using Online Portfolio. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title News and Public Relations Writer/Editor Department Office of University Communication-0852 Requisition Number S_260445 Posting Open Date 06/08/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 06/26/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Reporting to the senior director of strategic communications, this position serves as a primary editorial partner for the university’s news and strategic communications operation. This role supports the university’s strategic communication efforts by contributing advanced editorial expertise to the creation, coordination and dissemination of news and information that enhances the institution’s reputation, engages key stakeholders and aligns with university goals. Working closely with the senior director of strategic communications, this position provides continuity for day-to-day newsroom operations and exercises delegated editorial authority in support of established priorities. The role requires exceptional news judgment, strong collaboration skills and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced newsroom environment. Please include 3-5 examples of authored stories or link to online portfolio with application. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Journalism, Communication, English or related field plus two years professional experience in a newsroom, agency or for an organization conducting public relations and communications. Ability to identify and seek sources for news stories necessary. Ability to develop communication strategy and management functions essential. Must have knowledge of and experience using Associated Press style. Experience in converging new technologies in news delivery such as new media and social networking technologies helpful necessary. Preferred Qualifications Five years experience working for a news organization desirable. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $60,000/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Please attach 3-5 examples of authored stories or a link as one document using Online Portfolio. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Troy Fedderson TFEDDERSON@UNL. EDU 402-472-8515 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Online Portfolio Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102105": {
      "title": "Marketing Associate",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Marketing Associate Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Marketing Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Marketing Associate Department University Press-0933 Requisition Number S_260713 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The University of Nebraska Press ( UNP ), founded in 1941, is the largest university press between Chicago and California. It publishes scholarly and general-interest books (with more than 5,000 titles in print and an additional 120 new titles released each year) and journals (with more than 30 different journals published each year) in topics ranging from anthropology and literary criticism to history and sports. The Marketing Associate manages and creates content for all social media accounts for the Press. Assists marketing and sales manager with special projects related to online promotions, author requests, and design projects. Manages award submissions. Coordinates with publicity on sharing review coverage to Press networks. Assists the marketing department with ongoing tactics as needed, including blurb outreach and other communications. This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite program. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Proficient experience in Microsoft Office and standard suite of MS tools. Ability to organize multiple tasks simultaneously and meet tight deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Experience in book publishing, preferably scholarly publishing. Excellent communicative skills highly desired. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Ember Welsch ewelsch2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please detail your proficient experience in Microsoft Office and standard suite of MS tools. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/97613": {
      "title": "Food Service Associate (On-Call; Curtis, NE)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Food Service Associate (On-Call; Curtis, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Food Service Associate (On-Call; Curtis, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Food Service Associate (On-Call; Curtis, NE) Department NE College of Technical Agriculture-0928 Requisition Number S_250566 Posting Open Date 07/15/2025 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Nebraska College of Technical Agriculture ( NCTA ), located in Curtis, NE, is nationally ranked as one of the best two-year colleges, and Forbes Business Magazine placed us among the top 30 trade schools in the nation. Our programs have high academic quality, are affordable and guarantee career success for graduates. Position Overview NCTA is seeking a reliable, customer-focused Food Service Associate to serve in a flexible, on-call capacity . Work hours may be scheduled in advance or requested on an as-needed basis, depending on operational needs. Duties and Responsibilities Perform a variety of food service tasks across cafeteria, deli, catering, and related areas. Set up and close down stations; cook, prep ingredients, and restock supplies. Maintain food quality and presentation standards; monitor temperature, taste, and appearance. Operate dish machines and perform general cleaning and light custodial duties. Control food costs and waste; assist with inventory and recipe prep. Provide excellent customer service and assist with cashiering and computer use. Train others as needed; perform additional duties as assigned. Position requires obtaining a Food Handler’s permit (can be earned by passing Safety and Sanitation test). Position requires the ability to push/pull heavy carts that may exceed 50 pounds and requires lifting and moving of heavy items, including on stairs. On-Call employees may work up to 693 hours per fiscal year and are not eligible for paid leave or any other university benefits. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as O/S On Call Hourly. The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications High school or equivalent experience, plus one year of experience in a work environment required. Ability to read, write, weigh and measure necessary. Ability to learn food service techniques and use of equipment essential. Customer service skills required. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Experience in cafeteria and deli food service operations. Knowledge of ServeSafe guidelines. Familiarity with cash registers and money handling. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $15.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Kari Eidenmueller keidenmueller2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Part-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Curtis, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101655": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Catering Prep Chef/Driver Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Catering Prep Chef/Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Catering Prep Chef/Driver Department Housing: Catering-12429 Requisition Number S_260625 Posting Open Date 08/06/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/18/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Catering Prep Chef/Driver is an integral member of the catering team. This position will assist the entire Catering department. In this role you will: Safely operate the catering box truck, or other University vehicles in all weather conditions. Oversee and execute the pickup, drop off and delivery of food, materials, and equipment necessary for events. Support the culinary and front of house teams with operational assistance, including food preparation, dishwashing, event set up, tear down, and clean up. Ensure the Catering vehicles are following proper maintenance schedules in accordance with University protocols. Have a customer service focus, ability to utilizes effective time management skills, and a strong attention to detail with high accuracy are vital to this position. Schedule varies and includes early morning, evenings, late night, and weekend shifts. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications 8th grade education and 3 years of driving with the ability to drive a box truck; equivalent education/experience considered. Ability to read, write, weigh and measure necessary. Flexibility, reliability, ability to communicate and be a team player essential. Accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent customer service skills, oral and written communication skills, and the ability to work with a variety of individuals. Ability to safely operate a delivery vehicle. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirement and the ability to pass a DMV check authorizing them to operate university vehicles. Food Handlers Permit or ability to obtain upon employment required. Preferred Qualifications Experience driving a box truck. Experience working in a fast paced ever changing environment. Knowledge of University operations. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jacob Dietrich jdietrich3@unl.edu 4024726828 Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Early morning, evenings, late night, and weekend shifts. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have 3 years of driving experience? Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102007": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Paleontology Collection Manager Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Paleontology Collection Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Paleontology Collection Manager Department University Museum-0932 Requisition Number S_260369 Posting Open Date 05/19/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 06/12/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Principal responsibilities are organization, management, preservation, conservation, and supervision of use of paleontological specimens in the collections of the UNSM Paleontology Department, including the Invertebrate Paleontology and Vertebrate Paleontology Divisions. This position also maintains archives related to the collections and other important documents. Responsibilities include maintenance of the Paleontology databases and collection digitization – photography, data records, archived catalogues, field notebooks, and additional metadata (provenance, identifications, etc.). Duties include monitoring the storage environment and security, monitoring for pests and taking appropriate pest management actions, conducting object condition reports, coordinating incoming and outgoing loans, and processing new acquisitions. This position assists and supervises visiting researchers, trains and supervises collection volunteers, UNL student interns, student employees, nonstudent employees and other users of the collections in collaboration with paleontology staff and curators to ensure proper maintenance of collections. An additional set of responsibilities centers on supporting the museum’s public education mission by assisting with exhibit curation (selection of objects, drafting text, installing/de-installing exhibit objects), assisting with educational programs as a content expert and speaker, and contributing to the museum’s digital presence by providing content for social media posts and website. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Paleontology, geology, earth sciences, museum studies or related field and 3 years’ experience in managing museum collections, including knowledge of professional practices in object care, documentation, loans, exhibitions, packing and shipping; additional years of completed relevant education may substitute on a year-for-year basis. Working knowledge of databases and standard MS office software proficiency (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Supervisory experience. Knowledge of and past experience in securing federal or state permits to comply with federal Paleontological Resources Preservation Act ( PRPA ) and relevant state laws. Museum collections management skills. Knowledge of professional practices in object care, object reports, archives and other documentation, loans, exhibitions, packing and shipping. Knowledge of taxonomic principles. Ability to follow policies and procedures regarding sensitive data and maintain confidentiality. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications PHD in Paleontology, geology, earth sciences, museum studies or related field Working knowledge of Specify and Filemaker Pro databases. Experience working with paleontology field crews and communities. Knowledge of Native American Graves and Repatriation Act ( NAGPRA ) and its relevance to archaeological and adjoining paleontological sites. Demonstrated experience writing exhibit text, exhibit curation; or experience collaborating with educators as a content expert and providing appropriate text or references for curriculum Experience working with undergraduate students or graduate students. Experience supporting faculty and curator research needs. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $51,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Ember Welsch, Human Resources Specialist Lead Office of Research and Innovation ewelsch2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101222": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Feedlot Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Feedlot Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Feedlot Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260537 Posting Open Date 07/14/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 07/24/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Feedlot Hand, you will: Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area. Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 6,500 head at the feedlot. Maintain pens, machinery and fences. Collect research data. Experience in the care and riding of horses preferred but not required. Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between feeding locations and facilities is required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a pen rider or feed truck driver. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma plus one year beef livestock production experience required; equivalent education/experience will be considered. Precision, accuracy, and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain and operate equipment associated with feedlot operation. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Ability to care for, saddle, and ride horses to sort individual animals from groups in a feedlot pen setting. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with the care and management of cattle, including both paid and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations).  Make sure to include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102179": {
      "title": "Finance Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Finance Specialist - HAPPI Business Center Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Finance Specialist - HAPPI Business Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Finance Specialist - HAPPI Business Center Department HAPPI Business Center-3027 Requisition Number S_260725 Posting Open Date 09/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/23/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The HAPPI Business Center is a collaborative team providing specialized business services that advance the teaching, research, and extension missions of our partner units. As a Finance Specialist , you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions. Responsibilities include: Managing an assigned portfolio, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources which may include state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts. Supporting sponsored research through post-award grant financial management and administration. Providing consultative guidance on university financial policies, sponsored programs, and business processes, helping departments navigate complex issues and identify practical, compliant solutions. Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions. We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service. This position is located on UNL’s East Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on site. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs. Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. About Us At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Ample paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Employee & dependent scholarship program to pursue higher education Generous retirement plans with university match Learn more about UNL benefits and your total compensation at: https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus (4) years of related experience in financial management, accounting, grant administration, or related field. Equivalent education/experience considered. Experience working with SAP or another large integrated financial system. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite or similar software, including Excel for data analysis and reporting, and the ability to learn and use new technologies. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information in compliance with applicable laws, regulations, and university policies. Strong communication skills and the ability to build positive, collaborative relationships with a variety of stakeholders. Excellent organizational skills with the ability to prioritize work, manage multiple deadlines, and adapt in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Experience with grant, project, or cost accounting. Experience providing consultative support, training, or mentoring. Experience in a higher education environment. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $51,961/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jodi Mackin jmackin1@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have any experience with SAP or another fully integrated electronic human resources, financial management or payroll system? If yes, please describe. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (or similar software). (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100595": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Open Rank Geoscientist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Geoscientist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job” and then “Faculty Application.” Complete the application and attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes a) your qualifications for the job; b) anticipated contributions to research and extension; and c) a statement describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to environments where every person and every interaction matters (2-page maximum). See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Open Rank Geoscientist Department School of Natural Resources-0844 Requisition Number F_260058 Posting Open Date 05/22/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 06/24/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The School of Natural Resources ( SNR ) Conservation and Survey Division ( CSD ) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) is seeking applications for an open rank geoscientist position. This 12-month (calendar year), non-tenure track appointment will develop a research program and educate the public on issues related to groundwater resources and the hydrogeology of Nebraska and the surrounding region. Located in Lincoln, Nebraska, the apportionment is 75% research and 25% extension. Specific Duties Research (75%) Build and maintain a successful applied research program with innovative and complimentary water related focus ( https://snr.unl.edu/csd/ ). Plan and conduct basic and applied research on hydrogeology and geology. Generate external research grants. Collaborate with governmental agencies, municipalities, industry, and educational institutions. Develop and maintain working relationships with stakeholders to address water-related research and issues. Respond to inquiries by evaluating and interpreting data and applying current research understandings. Present findings at various venues including seminars, workshops, guest lectures, and national scientific meetings. Extension (25%) Publish manuscripts and present on groundwater issues in Nebraska to the appropriate audiences. Educate the public and stakeholders on groundwater issues. Support the CSD team’s survey efforts and mission with expert interactions and reporting (Annual Groundwater levels report). Work in conjunction with SNR Geology, Soil, and Water Survey faculty to provide services to clientele. Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) and the School of Natural Resources Conservation and Survey Division are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications M.S in geology, hydrology, environmental sciences, or a closely related field at the time of appointment. A valid United States driver’s license at the time of appointment. Demonstrated potential to produce scientific work, including peer-reviewed manuscripts with expertise in water quality, water quantity, or modeling commensurate with career level. Demonstratable analytical and quantitative skills applicable to understanding groundwater issues relevant to Nebraska and the region. Excellent oral and written communication skills applicable to communication with a variety of stakeholders. Ability to engage in scientific teamwork in order to address major issues. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in geology, hydrology, environmental sciences, or a closely related field at the time of appointment. Understanding of water issues such as aquifer characterization, groundwater-surface water interactions, groundwater quality and quantity in agriculture landscapes, impacts of a changing climate on groundwater systems, vadose zone processes, or emerging methods or techniques in groundwater science. Demonstrated experience in computational techniques, cyberinfrastructure, field methods, hydrogeophysics, or hydrogeologic mapping. Record of success in external funding. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job” and then “Faculty Application.” Complete the application and attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes a) your qualifications for the job; b) anticipated contributions to research and extension; and c) a statement describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to environments where every person and every interaction matters (2-page maximum). See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jodi Mackin jmackin1@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type 12 Month (Faculty Only) Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101828": {
      "title": "Instructional Services Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Instructional Services Coordinator Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructional Services Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. THIS POSTING IS FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES ONLY . To apply, interested applicants should go to University of Nebraska System’s employment website: https://jobs.nebraska.edu/UniversityNebraskaSystem/go/University-of-Nebraska-System/9756900/ or Click here to apply: https://jobs.nebraska.edu/UniversityNebraskaSystem/job/Instructional-Services-Coordinator/2028-en_US Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Instructional Services Coordinator Department University of Nebraska System Requisition Number S_260668 Posting Open Date 08/17/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Provide project and Instructional Services clerical support to all initiatives involving the University of Nebraska High School. Support includes inter- and intra-departmental, external client and vendor project and or program organization, coordination, communications, maintenance, and tracking to ensure all projects and student support items are effectively completed on-time. Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. #LI-DNI Minimum Required Qualifications Two years post-secondary coursework 2 years experience in office management, logistics, communication, customer service or related experience. Experience using Microsoft suite, especially Excel and Word Equivalent combination of education and experience, that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities may be considered. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Demonstrated experience in project management, business analysis, and change management Experience in a higher education environment The ideal candidate is an agile professional with strong interpersonal communication skills, flexibility and responsiveness; exhibits high ethical standards; proficient in managing time and competing priorities; responsive and committed to supporting, and motivating staff; committed to the ideals of a major public research university. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $37,600/yr minimum How to Apply THIS POSTING IS FOR INFORMATION PURPOSES ONLY . To apply, interested applicants should go to University of Nebraska System’s employment website: https://jobs.nebraska.edu/UniversityNebraskaSystem/go/University-of-Nebraska-System/9756900/ or Click here to apply: https://jobs.nebraska.edu/UniversityNebraskaSystem/job/Instructional-Services-Coordinator/2028-en_US For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Direct questions about the position to: humanresources@nebraska.edu Direct questions about the on-line application process to: 402-472-3701 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
