    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101231": {
      "title": "Graduate Admission Support Associate (Temporary)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Graduate Admission Support Associate (Temporary) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Admission Support Associate (Temporary) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Graduate Admission Support Associate (Temporary) Department Graduate Studies-0900 Requisition Number S_260522 Posting Open Date 07/15/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 07/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work This is a temporary data entry and online customer service position that supports the processing of electronic applications for graduate study at UNL . The responsibilities of this position are essential to maintain the integrity and continuity of key quality control functions related to admissions data. Accurate and timely data entry at the point of application is critical, as it directly impacts identity management, enrollment, student accounts, and university reporting. Ensuring these data points are correctly entered at the start of the student-university relationship is vital to the institution’s operational and reporting accuracy. The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 1 year of experience in an administrative, clerical, or data entry role; Additional years of relevant experience may substitute for education on a year-for-year basis. Proficient in general computer use and common software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office) Demonstrated ability to quickly learn new data systems and processes Excellent critical thinking and problem-solving skills to identify errors and resolve discrepancies in the data Proven experience in accurate and efficient data entry Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Excellent verbal and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications 3 years of experience in an administrative, clerical, or data entry role. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $19.330/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Mary Ashbury mashbury3@unl.edu 402-472-9539 Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Temporary Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: ASAP Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please detail your experience in an administrative, clerical, or data entry role, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your proficiency in general computer use and common software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office). (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your experience in accurate and efficient data entry, while identifying errors and resolving discrepancies in the data. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your experience in jobs that have required independence, strong organizational skills, and good communication skills. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101891": {
      "title": "Associate Director",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Associate Director Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Associate Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Associate Director Department Admissions-0959 Requisition Number S_260451 Posting Open Date 06/09/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/03/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Associate Director leads undergraduate admissions recruitment for first-time freshmen both nationally and within Nebraska. This role coordinates high school visits, college fairs, and outreach with counselors and educators outside Nebraska in primary, secondary, and tertiary markets, under the guidance of the Executive Director of Admissions. The Office of Admissions is part of the Academic Services and Enrollment Management ( ASEM ) division. As a member of the Admissions Leadership Team, the Associate Director collaborates with peers across the division, leveraging data to guide recruitment efforts and provide leadership to achieve enrollment goals. Responsibilities include analyzing graduation rates in states bordering Nebraska and in key markets. The Associate Director oversees a recruitment team and directly supervises Assistant Directors. They guide staff to meet enrollment goals and provide regular progress updates to the Executive Director of Admissions. Key responsibilities include training staff in territory management, monitoring performance, and supporting professional growth. This role plans and implements yield activities and territory strategies to convert prospects into enrollments. The Associate Director reviews recruitment data and territory outcomes, making data-driven adjustments to strengthen strategies and increase market share. In collaboration with the Executive Director, Admissions Leadership, and campus partners, the Associate Director develops reports and plans to drive strategy and achieve enrollment targets. The Associate Director exercises independent judgment in interpreting admissions policies, making recruitment decisions, and overseeing functional initiatives aligned with strategic priorities. The position collaborates with units within ASEM and across campus to align recruitment objectives with university initiatives. Additionally, the Associate Director works closely with Visitor Experience to ensure effective resource allocation for recruitment events and activities, and builds strong relationships with high school counselors, community contacts, and key influencers to expand student access and support recruitment. As needed, this role provides leadership support to the broader admissions team and may serve as a proxy for the Executive Director of Admissions. Regular travel, including evenings and weekends, is required. This position is based in Lincoln, Nebraska, and provides leadership for the national recruitment team, with travel to key recruitment markets across the country expected. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 4 years of professional experience in recruitment, enrollment management, admissions, enrollment marketing, or other related fields Demonstrated experience in public speaking and delivering presentations Experience supervising professional staff, including responsibility for performance management and team development Experience using Salesforce or another customer relationship management ( CRM )system to inform strategy and track outcomes Ability to analyze and interpret recruitment or enrollment data to inform strategic decisions Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports and present information to stakeholders Knowledge of undergraduate admissions recruitment, operations and procedures Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build relationships with a variety of stakeholders Event planning and coordination skills Proven ability to work independently with minimal supervision or administrative support Willingness to travel Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Demonstrated leadership of cross-departmental recruitment initiatives or strategic enrollment projects Track record of achieving or exceeding enrollment targets at a mid- to large-size public university Proficiency in territory management and yield strategy within an admissions setting Skill in organizing or facilitating large-scale recruitment events or outreach programs Strong background in training and mentoring professional staff in admissions recruitment Knowledge of the state of Nebraska and the University of Nebraska–Lincoln ( UNL ) Experience in national recruitment at a large public university Familiarity with UNL’s high school and college relations operations and procedures Knowledge of high-achieving student recruitment strategies In-depth knowledge of UNL and its enrollment landscape Familiarity with UNL’s University Honors Programs Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $70,000/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sandy Airan, sairan2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid driver's License? Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102113": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (10:30pm-7:00am, Weds-Sun) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (10:30pm-7:00am, Weds-Sun) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (10:30pm-7:00am, Weds-Sun) Department Campus Recreation-0965 Requisition Number S_260720 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings. In this role you will: Performs routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities Maintains offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers Ensures a clean, safe environment for all guests Cleans hard floors and carpets Mixes cleaning solutions as directed Assists with event setup and conference operations as needed The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications. Depending upon level assigned, this position may: Train and oversee work of others Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment Order supplies When hired as a Hospitality Services Attendant , the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development. When hired as a Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level. Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications 8th grade Ability to follow written and oral instructions. Must have the ability to understand cleaning chemicals and their application and dilution rations. Must have the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds. Must be available via cell phone during working hours. Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent experience preferred. Previous custodial experience preferred. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Salary commensurate with experience How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Gabe Nelson gnelson4@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) 10:30pm-7:00am, Weds-Sun Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: 9/27/2026 Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
