    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102119": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260719 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will: Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area. Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle. Maintain machinery and fences, Assist with pasture management Assist with the collection of research data. Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position may be referred to as a herdsman or cowboy. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about UNL benefits and your total compensation at: https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma plus one year beef livestock production experience required; equivalent education/experience considered. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain equipment, machinery, fields and pastures essential. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet UNL driver eligibility. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with the care and management of livestock animals, including both paid and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations).  Make sure to include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99958": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Seasonal Staff Positions (North Platte, NE; Temporary) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Seasonal Staff Positions (North Platte, NE; Temporary) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Seasonal Staff Positions (North Platte, NE; Temporary) Department West Central Research, Extension and Education Center-0944 Requisition Number S_260154 Posting Open Date 03/02/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The West Central Research, Extension and Education Center ( WCREEC ) in North Platte, NE seeks motivated individuals to fill temporary seasonal roles in a variety of positions, including: Groundskeeping Performing basic outdoor grounds maintenance and landscaping duties. Facilities maintenance and custodial Performing basic building or facility maintenance tasks such as painting, cleaning indoor or outdoor areas, repairing fences. Farm/Crops Research Assistant Perform basic crop management tasks including planting, weeding, data collection. Livestock Research Assistant Perform basic livestock management tasks including feeding, watering, cleaning pens. Must be at least 18 years of age. Full- and part-time positions available. Applications are continuously reviewed. Within the UNL system, these positions are categorized as Temporary Office/Service Hourly positions. Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Temporary employees appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50 FTE ) or greater. Benefits for eligible temporary employees include the following: health, dental, vision, and life insurance. As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ Minimum Required Qualifications Eighth grade education required. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. All UNL employees must be at least 16 years of age. Many positions require that staff be at least 18 years of age, due to the duties of the position. Many positions require a pre-employment physical and/or valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Varies by position How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Kari Eidenmueller, kari.eidenmueller@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Temporary Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) North Platte, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Will be determined by unit needs. Planned Hire Date: As soon as possible. Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you at least 16 years of age? Yes No * Are you at least 18 years of age? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? YES NO * What type of work are you interested in performing? (select all that apply) Groundskeeping Facilities maintenance and custodial Crop Research Assistant Livestock Research Assistant * Please describe any paid or unpaid experience you have working in your indicated area of interest (groundskeeping, facilities, crops, livestock). (Open Ended Question) * Are you interested in full-time temporary positions? Yes No * Are you interested in part-time temporary positions? Yes No * If  you are interested in part-time temporary positions, please indicate the days and hours  you would be available to work. (Open Ended Question) If you are interested in working for a specific program or faculty member indicate that information here. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101707": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator (2 Positions Available)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Program Coordinator (2 Positions Available) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Program Coordinator (2 Positions Available) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Program Coordinator (2 Positions Available) Department Undergraduate Programs-2975 Requisition Number S_260641 Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/24/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The William H. Thompson Scholars ( WHT ) Learning Community provides academic and life skills support to recipients of the Susan Thompson Buffett Foundation Scholarship at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Grounded in the Ecology of Validation model, scholars are given opportunities to connect closely with staff, faculty, and peers through a sequence of shared academic courses, learning community activities, and advising. WHT is an energetic and student success focused environment, with Program Coordinators primarily focusing on providing support through individualized meetings with program scholars throughout the academic year. Working collaboratively with program staff to uphold the mission and core values of the WHT program, a Program Coordinator utilizes a holistic approach to support scholars in academics, personal wellness, social development, and professional development. Program Coordinators oversee individualized academic probation programming, connecting closely with at-promise scholars. Staff are responsible for teaching several sections of a first-year seminar course during the fall term and assist with the training and supervision of a peer mentor team. In addition to student support duties, Program Coordinators are assigned leadership responsibilities in areas such as: program diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts, social engagement, event planning, housing, study cafe, tutoring services, and education abroad. Administrative experience with maintaining databases is preferred. Peer mentors have mobile accessibility outside of the normal working hours and community programming occasionally require night or weekend obligations. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus 2 years of relevant experience required. Ability to organize and implement student-based programs necessary. Experience working with college students, specifically at-promise, essential. Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Three years of student services experience desirable. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $43,000/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jocelyn Bullock William H. Thompson Scholars Learning Community – Director jbullock6@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Attendance of events/trainings outside business hrs may be required Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102016": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260672 Posting Open Date 08/19/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/28/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will: Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area. Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle. Maintain machinery and fences. Assist with pasture management and the collection of research data. Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy. Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this positon. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency plus one year livestock production experience required; additional relevant education may substitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain equipment, machinery, fields and pastures essential. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet UNL driver eligibility. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with the care and management of livestock animals, including both paid and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations).  Make sure to include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101608": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Passport Agent Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Passport Agent Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Passport Agent Department Passport Office-10100 Requisition Number S_260524 Posting Open Date 08/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/12/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The passport agent will oversee and execute the passport application process and ensure all materials and documents needed to process the application are correctly submitted. The agent works independently screening evidence of U.S. Citizenship, recording application identification documentation, collecting and forwarding required passport fees and securing all personal identity information along with federal documents. Greeting applicants/customers, directing customers to desired service areas, assisting walk-in applicants using a computer based scheduling software and other duties as assigned. At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Ample paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life Employee & dependent scholarship program to pursue higher education Generous retirement plans with a university match The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in business administration or related field plus minimum 2 years of clerical/office experience or related field required; equivalent education/experience considered. Must have basic level computer proficiency with the ability to use email and internet, word processing and spreadsheet software, maintain digital files, and cash handling experience. Must be able to demonstrate excellent customer service and communication skills along with the ability to work in a fast-paced environment requiring a high level of multi-tasking. Ability to work under pressure and unsupervised required. Ability to obtain Passport Acceptance Agent Certification within one week of start date. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration or a related field preferred. Passport experience preferred. Passport Acceptance Agent Certification previously obtained desirable. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $16.50/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Gina Kroger GINA .KROGER@UNL. EDU Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your computer proficiency with the following: email and internet, word processing and spreadsheet software and maintaining digital files. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your cash handling experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your clerical/office experience (or related field), including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your ability to pay attention to detail and work independently while completing tasks in a fast-paced work environment. (Open Ended Question) * Are you a US citizen or a UN non-citizen national as required by the Bureau of Consular affairs? Yes No * Are you at least 18 years of age? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever been convicted or pled guilty to a felony? Yes No * Have you ever been convicted/indicted for any Federal, State or local misdemeanor involving breach of trust, dishonesty, or crimes of moral turpitude, including but not limited to:\r\no\tEmbezzlement \r\no\tIdentity theft \r\no\tMisappropriation \r\no\tDocument fraud \r\no\tDrug offenses \r\no\tDishonesty involving responsibilities of public trust (Open Ended Question) * Are you presently on parole or probation related to any Federal, State, or local convictions? (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
