    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101992": {
      "title": "Residence Director",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Residence Director Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Residence Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Residence Director Department Housing: Residence Directors-11951 Requisition Number S_260678 Posting Open Date 08/21/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/03/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Residence Director is vital for engaging with students that live in residence halls at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Residence Directors are empowered to connect with their residential community to help students become engaged members of the community and to thrive as students at UNL with the goal of achieving graduation. An individual in this position will serve on a dynamic team of professionals that work together at a Big 10 institution to implement the Nebraska Residential Experience curriculum framework. As a Residence Director you will: Focus on student success, engagement, and leadership. Oversee daily operations of a residence hall. Lead a team of student leaders. Gain valuable experience in a multitude of areas including community engagement, supervision, crisis response, leadership development, and summer conferences. Participate in departmental committees, collaborate across campus and build partnerships and contribute to the campus mission. Strong communication, collaboration, creativity, and adaptability are essential qualities for a Residence Director. This role encourages providing feedback on department and campus initiatives, expanding knowledge on best practices to support college students, and offers professional development opportunities. Residence Directors collaborate within a large department, making collective decisions, and ensuring an optimal residential experience for University of Nebraska-Lincoln students. In the summer, the role extends to community engagement through conference services. This multifaceted position emphasizes personal and professional growth within a supportive and collaborative environment. This position is considered essential, and schedules include office hours, some evenings, weekends, and being available in an on-call rotation. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and one year of leadership experience in a student housing employment position. Demonstrated experience leading a team of college students. Ability to communicate and work well with others. Proficiency with Microsoft Office software and e-mail systems. Strong written and oral communication skills are essential. Preferred Qualifications Masters Degree in Student Affairs, College Student Personnel Administration, or related field. Two or more years of direct supervision of live-in Resident Assistants Two or more years of full time Residence Hall Director experience Participation in professional staff on call duty rotation Hall government advising experience Experience with budgeting Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $43,890/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Rob Andrews III randrews@unl.edu 402-472-3872 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Includes Evening and Weekend Hours Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102191": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Associate Registrar Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Associate Registrar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Associate Registrar Department Office of the University Registrar-0961 Requisition Number S_260696 Posting Open Date 09/08/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Associate Registrar provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the Office of the University Registrar’s academic services. This position directs the administration of curriculum management, class scheduling, enrollment services, graduation and degree certification, and the management of general-purpose classroom assignments. The Associate Registrar ensures these services are delivered efficiently, accurately, and in compliance with institutional policies while supporting student success and timely degree completion. The position supervises curricular services staff and provides leadership to the Assistant Registrar responsible for the Academic Services Specialist team. Through effective supervision, staff development, and process improvement initiatives, the Associate Registrar promotes operational excellence and high-quality service to students, faculty, advisors, and academic administrators. Serving as the primary liaison between the Office of the University Registrar and the university’s colleges and academic units regarding operations, the Associate Registrar works collaboratively with campus stakeholders to address curricular, scheduling, enrollment, and graduation-related needs. As a member of the University Curriculum Committee, the Associate Registrar provides expertise on curricular governance and system support. The Associate Registrar directs registrar-related activities associated with commencement ceremonies held three times annually, coordinating degree certification processes and serving as the Office of the University Registrar’s representative on the University Commencement Committee. The position ensures accurate degree conferral and successful commencement operations, contributing to an exceptional experience for graduates and their families. The position provides functional leadership for registrar technologies supporting curricular and academic services operations. Working closely with information technology and programming staff, the Associate Registrar implements system enhancements and tests new functionality. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of experience working with university curriculum and degree programs required. Must have excellent communication and writing skills. Experience working with individuals at all levels of an institution necessary. Must have extensive knowledge of Registrar’s office procedures and processes. Ability to clearly provide direction to office staff and external partners in proper operations and procedures essential. General knowledge of college degree requirements and how university work is accomplished required. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in education, business, MIS or related field More than 5 years of progressive and related full-time employment experience desirable. Preferred ability to effectively communicate with senior campus leadership in a clear and concise manner. Ability to build relationships with campus units and promote the Office of the University Registrar’s services helpful. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $72,000/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sandy Airan, sairan2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101035": {
      "title": "Hospitality Service Associate (4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Hospitality Service Associate (4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Hospitality Service Associate (4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Hospitality Service Associate (4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon) Department Campus Recreation-0965 Requisition Number S_260499 Posting Open Date 06/30/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 07/13/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings. In this role you will: Performs routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities Maintains offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers Ensures a clean, safe environment for all guests Cleans hard floors and carpets Mixes cleaning solutions as directed Assists with event setup and conference operations as needed The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications. Depending upon level assigned, this position may: Train and oversee work of others Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment Order supplies When hired as a Hospitality Services Attendant , the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development. When hired as a Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level. Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. Minimum Required Qualifications Eighth grade education or equivalent required. Ability to follow written and oral instructions. Ability to follow written and oral instructions. Must have the ability to understand cleaning chemicals and their application and dilution rations. Must have the ability to provide excellent customer service. Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds. Must be available via cell phone during working hours. Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent experience preferred. Previous custodial experience preferred. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Salary commensurate with experience How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Gabe Nelson gnelson4@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) 4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: July 30, 2026 Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101875": {
      "title": "Associate RDN (Registered Dietitian/Nutritionist)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Associate RDN (Registered Dietitian/Nutritionist) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Associate RDN (Registered Dietitian/Nutritionist) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Associate RDN (Registered Dietitian/Nutritionist) Department Athletics-0850 Requisition Number S_260662 Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/24/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Associate RDN provides comprehensive nutrition services to the University of Nebraska Athletic Department and serves as a senior performance nutrition practitioner within the department. Primary responsibilities include developing, implementing, and evaluating nutrition strategies for student-athletes; overseeing fueling stations and, supporting sports dietitians and the student internship program; and collaborating with nutrition, sports medicine, strength and conditioning, psychological services, food service, and team staffs. The Associate RDN serves as a nutrition resource for student-athletes, coaches, staff, prospective student-athletes and their families, and other athletic department partners. This position works independently within established departmental policies and professional standards and assists the Director of Olympic Performance Nutrition & Assistant AD for Performance Nutrition with program development, quality management, and continuous improvement. Perform any additional duties as assigned by the Director of Olympic Performance Nutrition & Assistant AD for Performance Nutrition. Must be able to work a non-standard work week which may include nights, weekends, holidays, and travel if needed with team. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Must have either: Bachelor’s degree in Nutrition or related field or Master’s degree in Nutrition or Master’s degree with DPD requirements 3 years of experience as a dietitian. Must be a Registered Dietitian Strong clinical skills in medical nutrition therapy Knowledge of performance nutrition principles and strategies Strong communication, interpersonal and team-oriented skills. Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced athletic environment. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Nutrition, dietetics or related field Collegiate or professional sports experience Experience supervising or mentoring dietitians, interns, graduate assistants, or students. Experience with fueling operations, team meals, travel nutrition, and performance nutrition program assessment. Strong public speaking skills with the ability to provide nutrition education information. CPR certified Serve Safe or Food Handlers Permit Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $90,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Abbie Herkelman aherkelman2@huskers.com Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
