    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101729": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Dispatcher (2 positions available) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Dispatcher (2 positions available) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Dispatcher (2 positions available) Department University Police-0823 Requisition Number S_260648 Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/18/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Are you someone who thrives under pressure, cares deeply about helping others, and enjoys using technology to solve real-world problems? Join our team as a Dispatcher and play a vital role in keeping our UNL community safe. You’ll be the critical link between callers in need and emergency responders—making a difference every shift. What You’ll Do Answer emergency and non-emergency calls for police, fire, and EMS services Use multi-line phones, radio systems, and computer-aided dispatch ( CAD ) tools to coordinate rapid response Communicate clearly and calmly with callers and first responders during high-stress situations Relay essential information to public safety officials and partner agencies Maintain accurate records and reports Complete six months of paid training What Makes You a Great Fit A strong commitment to serving your community Excellent customer service and communication skills Ability to stay calm, focused, and detail-oriented during urgent situations Interest in technology and learning new systems Skill at multitasking and adapting to frequent interruptions Familiarity with campus and city geography (helpful but not required) Ability to work a variety of schedules (overnights, weekends, special events, etc.) Why Join Us? Meaningful work that directly impacts community safety Opportunities to build valuable skills in communication, technology, and crisis response A supportive team environment where your professionalism and dedication are valued If you’re ready to be a steady voice in critical moments and serve your community with purpose, we encourage you to apply. About Us At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Employee & dependent scholarship program to pursue higher education Generous retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Experience with customer service and computers Typing speed of 30+ words per minute Valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria Preferred Qualifications Previous experience, training or coursework related to public safety or communications preferred but not required. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $22.491/hr How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Clayton Murray BFBCPoliceHR@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Varying shifts include days, nights, weekends, and holidays Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you used marijuana, or any derivatives, for any purpose, in the last two years? If yes, when was the last time? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a valid driver's license? YES NO * This position is part of a 24-hour, 7 day a week, 365 day a year operation, and will require working various shifts, weekends, and holidays. It also requires working special events. Do you have any concerns or reservations about this requirement? Explain. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter List of References Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
