    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101936": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Media Services Supervisor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Media Services Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Media Services Supervisor Department University Television-0912 Requisition Number S_260677 Posting Open Date 08/20/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Media Services Supervisor provides front-line technical and operational supervision for Nebraska Public Media’s Media Services department, including television, radio, and streaming traffic operations, underwriting contract services, metadata support, asset registration, and the Media Services Helpdesk. This position trains, supports, and supervises Media Services staff in the daily use of scheduling, automation, metadata, asset management, and related media delivery systems to ensure accurate broadcast logs, timely spot placement, reliable streaming support, and continuity of services. The position supports implementation of approved systems, workflows, and process changes; troubleshoots operational and technical issues; assists with rights management, playlist, distribution, and metadata compliance; and serves as a working supervisor to maintain operational coverage when needed. This role works under the direction of Media Operations leadership to ensure Media Services processes are carried out consistently, accurately, and in alignment with established standards and organizational needs. Nebraska Public Media offers a full spectrum of communications services to the citizens of Nebraska, the nation and the world. Some of these services include a nine-station, statewide noncommercial public television network affiliated with PBS ; a nine-station, statewide noncommercial public radio network affiliated with NPR ; a cutting-edge Digital Media Group; and state-of-the-art audio, video and multimedia production capability delivered via broadcast, satellite, cable, Internet and broadband delivery channels. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in broadcast engineering, media technology, information systems, business management, communications, or related field and three (3) years of experience in broadcast traffic, media operations, broadcast engineering support, or related environment. Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Knowledge of underwriting contract workflows, including availability, spot placement, inventory maintenance, performance affidavits, and contract fulfillment. Knowledge of metadata entry, asset registration, rights management, playlists, and distribution standards for broadcast and streaming platforms. Knowledge of broadcast automation, streaming, encoding, database systems, scheduling/traffic systems, and related technical infrastructure used in media operations. Ability to troubleshoot routine operational, scheduling, automation, streaming, metadata, and media delivery issues and escalate complex technical concerns as needed. Ability to supervise, train, support, and provide direction to staff. Ability to coordinate effectively with internal departments, vendors, and internal customers. Skill in Microsoft 365 applications, including Excel, sufficient to review reports, track workflow information, and support operational documentation. Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelors degree. Knowledge of ProTrack, PBS Edisen sIX, PBS Media Manager, EIDR , IMDb, YouTube, Media Pulse, remote support tools, or comparable media operations platforms. Knowledge of applicable State of Nebraska, University of Nebraska, FCC , industry, and organizational procedures related to Media Services operations. Ability to identify recurring workflow issues and recommend improvements to support accuracy, efficiency, service continuity, and customer support. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $55,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Humanresources@nebraskapublicmedia.org Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102139": {
      "title": "Director, International Student/Scholar Office",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Director, International Student/Scholar Office Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director, International Student/Scholar Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Director, International Student/Scholar Office Department Intl Student & Scholar Office-8401 Requisition Number S_260708 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Director of the International Student and Scholar Office ( ISSO ) serves as a member of the University of Nebraska-Lincoln’s global leadership team. The Director provides vision, oversight, and leadership to all areas of this comprehensive office: immigration advising, employment-based visas, sponsored students, and incoming exchange programs, to ensure that students and scholars maintain their legal status in the United States. ISSO also supports student engagement and intercultural initiatives to enhance student success, including significant programming dedicated to international students’ personal development and adjustment to UNL , in addition to leading programming that integrates international students, scholars, and their dependents. The Director oversees the delivery of exceptional services in all of these areas in collaboration with 7.5 professional staff who are all direct reports. Additional Duties: Provides vision, strategic management, expert policy interpretation and analysis, and leadership to the International Student & Scholar Office ( ISSO ); Serves as UNL’s Principal Designated School Official ( PDSO ) and Responsible Officer (RO) in overseeing the student and scholar programs in the government’s Student and Exchange Visitor Information System ( SEVIS ). Responsible for UNL’s participation in SEVIS and institutional compliance with federal immigration regulations. As such, oversees the training and support of Designated School Officials (DSOs) and Alternative Responsible Officers (AROs) on campus. Provides administrative leadership and oversight of ISSO operations, budgets, and personnel. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/. Minimum Required Qualifications Master’s in international education, international studies, student services, global affairs, higher education administration, comparative education, or related field plus 5 years of experience in an international student and scholar services role with direct experience processing F, J, H and other non-immigrant regulations required Three year’s experience leading effective teams. demonstrated knowledge of best practice in supporting international students and scholars in a university environment. excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication strong administrative, organizational, and collaborative leadership skills. Excellent leadership and supervisory skills Demonstrated experience developing immigration policies and procedures and knowledge of employment issues affecting international students and scholars. Proven ability to manage complex issues and competing priorities successfully Must be able to think creatively and solve problems effectively during periods of intense activity. Experience working successfully with international students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Technical experience with Student & Exchange Visitor Information System ( SEVIS ) and student information systems expected. Active involvement with NAFSA and/or other appropriate professional associations Must be a U.S. citizen or a U.S. Lawful Permanent Resident per federal regulations governing who can serve as a SEVIS Primary Designated School Official ( DSO ) for the Department of Homeland Security’s F visa program and the Responsible Officer (RO) for the Department of State’s BridgeUSA Exchange Visitor Program. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with UNL -specific software programs, including PeopleSoft and NUView. Experience with SUNAPSIS . Experience working within a large, decentralized university. Experience supporting and consulting on incidents or crises involving international students or scholars. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $85,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Maegan Stevens-Liska mstevens5@unl.edu 402-472-0743 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: 1/4/2027 Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100201": {
      "title": "Lecturer (German Language)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Lecturer (German Language) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer (German Language) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest describing your qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy. Attach as \"Other Document.\" In addition, candidates must arrange for three (3) letters of reference, one of which must focus on teaching, to be sent via email to Samantha Deline at sdeline2@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Lecturer (German Language) Department Modern Language & Literature-1090 Requisition Number F_260032 Posting Open Date 04/20/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 05/21/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at UNL seeks a full-time, one-year lecturer to teach German language and culture classes at the 100 (introductory) through 400 (advanced undergraduate) levels. The proposed load for the 2026-2027 academic year is eight (8) courses (approximately 24 credit hours) over two semesters. The proposed salary range is $42,000 (M.A.) – $45,000 (Ph.D.). The department is unable to sponsor visa applications for this position. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Master’s degree in German studies or a closely related field by August 2026. Professional-level proficiency in German and English. Experience teaching elementary and intermediate German in a university setting. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in German studies or a closely related field by August 2026. Experience teaching German culture courses in a university setting. Experience developing courses. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest describing your qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy. Attach as “Other Document.” In addition, candidates must arrange for three (3) letters of reference, one of which must focus on teaching, to be sent via email to Samantha Deline at sdeline2@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Lori Ratzlaff lratzlaff@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/17/2026 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101742": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Prototype Fabrication and Lab Manager Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Prototype Fabrication and Lab Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Prototype Fabrication and Lab Manager Department Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering-1058 Requisition Number S_260645 Posting Open Date 08/11/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/19/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is a dynamic, research-driven community advancing innovations across biomolecular engineering, nanotechnology, biotechnology, and molecular medicine. Students, staff, and faculty collaborate on cutting-edge, grant-funded research that addresses critical challenges in healthcare, sustainability, and advanced materials. As the Prototype Fabrication & Lab Manager, you will: Collaborate with faculty, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers to conceptualize, design, fabricate, and refine custom experimental apparatus that support novel research projects, where commercially available equipment may not exist. Assist with the design, fabrication, maintenance, and repair of laboratory equipment and devices. Ensure that the teaching and research labs in the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering meet the needs of the department, faculty, staff, and students. Coordinate with Environmental Health and Safety and OSHA to ensure compliance with all safety requirements and eliminate safety hazards. In the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Lab Mechanic. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in engineering technology or a related technical field plus one (1) year of technical experience using common machine shop and fabrication tools such as mills, lathes, drills, saws, grinders, hand tools, and precision measuring instruments; OR High school diploma or equivalent plus three (3) years of technical experience using common machine shop and fabrication tools such as mills, lathes, drills, saws, grinders, hand tools, and precision measuring instruments. Equivalent experience/education considered. Knowledge of equipment and machine maintenance and the design and fabrication of devices or equipment. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $26.17/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Noureddini hnoureddini1@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please detail your technical experience using common machine shop and fabrication tools such as mills, lathes, drills, saws, grinders, hand tools, and precision measuring instruments, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your knowledge of equipment and machine maintenance and the design and fabrication of devices or equipment. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101619": {
      "title": "Recruitment Coordinator & Academic Advisor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Recruitment Coordinator &amp; Academic Advisor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Recruitment Coordinator & Academic Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Recruitment Coordinator & Academic Advisor Department Biological Systems Engineering-0833 Requisition Number S_260606 Posting Open Date 07/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/18/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Biological Systems Engineering ( BSE ) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is a nationally recognized, comprehensive program with over 100 years of excellence in teaching, research, and extension. As a Recruitment Coordinator and Academic Advisor , you will: Create and implement a strategic plan for marketing and recruitment of students into the Agricultural Systems Technology, Agricultural Engineering, and Biological Systems Engineering majors. Conduct individual campus visits, school visits, and participate in statewide recruitment events to promote the Department and recruit prospective and transfer students. Build and maintain strong relationships with high schools, community colleges, counselors, teachers, Extension Educators, alumni, and industry. stakeholders to strengthen recruitment pipelines Coordinate on-campus recruitment activities and collaborate with the Recruitment Committee, Student Ambassadors, and other university partners to support engagement efforts. Advise undergraduate students in one or more of the assigned majors and support advising efforts across the Department. Provide support for recruits during the application and admission process, including new student enrollment, and manage the undergraduate recruitment data and reporting functions for the Department. Some travel is required, including evenings and weekends as needed for recruitment activities. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in science, engineering, technology, marketing or related field(s) plus two years of experience in recruiting, public relations, student services, sales, marketing or related field. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, and ability to utilize online platforms to provide advice/assistance to others. Valid driver’s license with ability to meet driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred, but not required: Familiarity with academic programs relevant to the position. Experience working in higher education, public relations, marketing, or related field. Marketing, recruitment or sales experience. Knowledge of university and college admissions procedures. Knowledge of relevant career opportunities for graduates. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $43,000/year minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Emma Gannon egannon4@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
