    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100334": {
      "title": "Co-Director",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Co-Director - Digital Research (Part-time, Open to CAS Faculty Only) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Co-Director - Digital Research (Part-time, Open to CAS Faculty Only) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Co-Director - Digital Research (Part-time, Open to CAS Faculty Only) Department College of Arts & Sciences-0906 Requisition Number F_260046 Posting Open Date 04/30/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 05/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work We seek applications and nominations for the CAS Co-Director of the Center for Digital Research in the Humanities ( CDRH ). The successful candidate will report to the CAS Dean at UNL , and the expected 1.0 FTE appointment will be split as 0.25 FTE administration with 0.75 FTE faculty. Primary areas of responsibility are shared with the Libraries CDRH Co-Director and will likely include: Administrative & Financial Leadership Oversee Center operations, consult on budgets, prepare required reports, and assume additional responsibilities consistent with the Center’s mission. Strategic Planning & Program Coordination Lead strategic planning efforts and provide overall coordination for Center programs, personnel, and space. Personnel Management & Evaluation Provide input on staff performance and faculty merit, reappointment, tenure, and promotion as requested or as required by appointment letters. Research, Teaching & Faculty Engagement Encourage and support CDRH Fellows’ research and teaching aligned with the Center’s mission, including consultation on funding opportunities. Advancement, Communication & Outreach Assist in fundraising efforts with University leadership; communicate Center activities and developments transparently to the CDRH community and relevant Deans. Governance & Representation Convene and chair Center meetings; represent the Center at College of Arts and Sciences Chairs and Directors meetings; report regularly to the Dean of UNL Libraries and the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Must be a current tenured faculty member in the College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln and a current CDRH Fellow. Demonstrable leadership ability, excellent interpersonal skills, and a vision for enhancing a center with a significant national and international reputation. Broad-ranging knowledge of the humanities and digital research in the humanities. Preferred Qualifications Department, College, or relevant Center leadership experience. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Carolyn Kollmann, ckollmann2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Academic Administrative Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/17/2026 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
