    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102108": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Electrician III (Ithaca, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Electrician III (Ithaca, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Electrician III (Ithaca, NE) Department Eastern Nebraska Research, Extension and Education Center-9750 Requisition Number S_260384 Posting Open Date 05/18/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Eastern Nebraska Research, Extension and Education Center ( ENREEC ) in Ithaca, Nebraska is a leading hub for agricultural research, education, and innovation. Spanning nearly 9,700 acres of row crops and pasture and home to over 6,000 livestock animals, ENREEC plays a vital role in advancing modern farming. ENREEC is located close to Mead, Fremont, Ashland, and Wahoo and is just 30 minutes from Omaha or Lincoln. As an Electrician III , you will: Install and maintain electrical power systems at ENREEC . Plan, perform, and supervise electrical installations including circuitry, sizing of wire, switching, mains and junction boxes for new and repair of existing single phase and three phase electrical systems. Perform diagnostics, repair, and maintenance on electrical equipment and controls. Prepare and obtain state electrical permits and perform follow-through inspections to ensure all electrical work is completed correctly and complies with current local, state and federal electrical codes. About Us Looking for a job where you can advance professionally and have time for life outside work? At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match A workplace culture that values your time outside of work Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency plus four (4) years of on-the-job electrical experience required. Additional completed relevant education may substitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Skilled in the maintenance, repair, and installation of electrical systems at the journeyman level. Current Journeyman Electrician license required. Proficient in basic computer applications, such as MS Office Suite, used for communication, scheduling, and collaboration. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Relevant coursework or specialized training beyond high school in electrical trade. Contractor or Masters Electrical License. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $27.40/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Darren Johnson, Facilities Mgr. 402-624-8016. Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Evenings and weekends may be required on occasion. Work Location (City, State) Ithaca, Nebraska Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list all current Licenses, Certifications and Qualifications you hold that are relevant to the Electrician III position. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe in detail your electrical experience and the amount of time you have been working in the electrical trade. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any other relevant construction or agricultural setting experience you may have. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/98837": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on the words “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. This posting will close December 31, 2026. If you wish to be considered in 2026, please apply under the posting titled 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool Department Human Resources-0821 Requisition Number S_260001 Posting Open Date 01/05/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Description of Work On occasion, the University of Nebraska is in need of highly motivated candidates who truly enjoy working with a wide variety of people. The ideal candidates will possess great customer service skills, a willingness to be flexible and good attention to detail. Duties could include: Filing, typing correspondence, data entry, phone/receptionist coverage, accounting, making travel arrangements, event planning assistance, and other duties as needed. A criminal history background check will be conducted. Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50FTE) or greater. Those appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits. Benefits for eligible temporary employees include the following: health, dental, vision and life insurance. As an EO/AA employer, qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See: http://www.unl.edu/equity/notice-nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High School plus two years clerical experience or equivalency. Must have basic computer experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience using Microsoft Word and Excel. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary How to Apply Click on the words “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. This posting will close December 31, 2026. If you wish to be considered in 2026, please apply under the posting titled 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Please call the employment office at 402-472-3101. Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Temporary Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Will be determined by individual department needs. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Will be determined by individual department needs. Planned Hire Date: A.S.A.P. Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you interested in full-time temporary positions? Yes No * Are you interested in part-time temporary positions? Yes No * If  you are interested in part-time temporary positions, please indicate the days and hours  you would be available to work. (Open Ended Question) * Are you interested in being considered for positions that are expected to last less than 6 months? Yes No * Please describe your experience using a multi-line telephone system. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the years of experience that you have with each of the following:  Excel, Access, Microsoft Word.  Please list any other programs that you are proficient using. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have direct customer service experience?  If so, please describe. (Open Ended Question) * Have you had any experience with Accounting?  If so, please describe. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101668": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260637 Posting Open Date 08/06/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/17/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will: Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area. Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle. Maintain machinery and fences. Assist with pasture management and the collection of research data. Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency plus one year livestock production experience required; additional relevant education may substitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain equipment, machinery, fields and pastures essential. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet UNL driver eligibility. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience working with livestock, including both paid employment and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations).  Make sure to include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102008": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Building/Grounds Attendant (5:00pm-2:00am) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Building/Grounds Attendant (5:00pm-2:00am) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Building/Grounds Attendant (5:00pm-2:00am) Department Lied Center for Performing Arts-0854 Requisition Number S_250377 Posting Open Date 06/04/2025 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 06/08/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Repairs and performs minor preventive maintenance on a variety of equipment. Performs a variety of duties in and around buildings and grounds. Performs assignments such as light bulb change and fixture and equipment cleaning, painting, carpentry: assists maintenance personnel and other workers with their tasks or projects. Perform building snow removal as required. Performs housekeeping and janitorial duties to maintain offices, restrooms and public areas in a clean and orderly condition. Mixes cleaning solutions to appropriate strength. Removes trash from offices and lobby areas. Perform room set ups and strikes. Follows established routine. Ability to read and understand cleaning instructions and information. Other duties as assigned. The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications High school plus one year commercial trades/maintenance experience or equivalency. General knowledge in a variety of skilled trades areas including plumbing, electrical, and carpentry. Ability to understand cleaning chemicals and their application and dilution ratios. Experience must demonstrate strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree in a relevant trades field. One year of custodial experience. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $16.50/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Natalie Stroud, nstroud2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) 40 hrs/wk-flexible schedule including days, nights, weekends Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please detail your commercial trades/maintenance experience, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your general knowledge in a variety of skilled trades areas including plumbing, electrical, and carpentry. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your organizational and communication skills. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
