    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101982": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Office Manager: Student Legal Services (9:00am-5:00pm, M-F) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Office Manager: Student Legal Services (9:00am-5:00pm, M-F) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Office Manager: Student Legal Services (9:00am-5:00pm, M-F) Department ASUN-1321 Requisition Number S_260691 Posting Open Date 08/24/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/02/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Ranked as one of the best employers in the state of Nebraska , the University of Nebraska is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. We invest in our employees: Vacation, sick, and holiday pay Medical, dental, and vision insurance No-cost life insurance Employee Assistance Program Retirement plans with University match Tuition assistance for full-time employees and dependents Exclusive staff discounts Continuous improvement and innovation Professional development through training and education And much more! The Office Manager is responsible for overseeing the administrative operations, supporting the director and attorneys with legal administrative support in the Student Legal Services office, and providing front-facing customer service. The Office Manager also provides assistance with budget and fiscal management. As Office Manager you will: Work with our students, staff and faculty who are requesting services or departmental information. Initiate and process confidential administrative case management by providing necessary documents and applications, correspondence on status, and update electronic files. Support the Director and attorneys by performing a combination of administrative and complex office work associated with the office, program administration, and data collection/entry. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s or equivalent education/experience with a minimum 2 years demonstrated administrative and/or office management experience. Demonstrated ability of and a well-developed working knowledge of Microsoft Office. Ability to prioritize and delegate work assignments while exercising the highest degree of confidentiality. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communications skills necessary. Must have good basic communication skills, both verbal and writing. Must have strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize work tasks. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in an environment with considerable interaction with people. Experience working within a legal office or working with matters that require a high degree of confidentiality, precision, and accuracy. Experience working with time-sensitive assignments and tasks. Experience working with college students, faculty, college staff (e.g., advisors, financial aid, student affairs, etc.). Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $23.69/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jeff White jwhite9@unl.edu 402-472-3350 Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) 9:00am-5:00pm, M-F Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please detail your administrative and/or office management experience, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience in jobs that have required strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience and ability in working with tasks that require attention to detail, accuracy and organizational skills. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
