    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102185": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Utility Operator Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Utility Operator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Utility Operator Department UO Husker Energy & Power-12300 Requisition Number S_260722 Posting Open Date 09/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. As a Utility Operator, you will: Assess daily steam, electricity, and chilled water load demands and identify and operate equipment to meet campus needs. Monitor plant equipment through observation, data analysis, and remote systems to ensure safe and reliable operation. Observe and interpret equipment conditions (sound, vibration, temperature, pressure, flow, electrical readings) and make necessary adjustments. Record data accurately in required written and electronic formats to meet regulatory and internal standards. Communicate with team members to support coordinated operations, such as detailed shift turnover information, equipment status, load changes, operational issues, and corrective actions. Submit and follow up on work orders for maintenance support. Assist maintenance personnel with preventive maintenance and equipment repairs. Husker Energy and Power has five levels of Utility Operator positions. Placement within a specific level is based on a candidate’s demonstrated knowledge, skills, abilities, relevant experience, and required licensure. Operators at higher levels are assigned expanded responsibilities and more complex duties aligned with the scope and expectations of that level. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications High school or equivalent experience. Ability to read and interpret operating manuals. Ability to understand and execute verbal and written instructions. Ability to perform basic mathematical computations. Ability to read, understand, follow, and enforce safety procedures. Skilled in the use of computer software for word processing, spreadsheets, data entry, and email communication. Ability to be available by telephone and work beyond the regular scheduled shift as needed, including 24/7 availability for emergencies, shift coverage, and operational needs. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree in Energy Generation Operations or a related field, or equivalent of two or more years of experience operating high-pressure boilers, centrifugal chillers, and/or related support systems in a comparable environment. Skilled in performing system inspections, making operational adjustments, and maintaining compliance with operating specifications. Skilled in the inspection, cleaning, adjustment, installation, repair, and replacement of utility plant equipment. Skilled in diagnosing and troubleshooting electrical, mechanical, and other equipment malfunctions, including emergency situations. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Salary commensurate with experience How to Apply Click on “Apply to this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Shea Kinnison, uopeopleops@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an Associate’s degree in Energy Generation Operations or a related field, or equivalent of two or more years of experience operating high-pressure boilers, centrifugal chillers, and/or related support systems in a comparable environment. Yes No Unsure Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100709": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Multispecies Livestock Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Multispecies Livestock Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Multispecies Livestock Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260422 Posting Open Date 05/29/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 06/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Multispecies Livestock Hand, you will: Work with and around cattle, pigs, and sheep. Be responsible for weighing, sorting, and animal health. Perform daily maintenance of machinery and fences. Treat sick animals. Feed livestock in the winter. Help with hay in the summer. Assist with collection of research data. This position requires some evening and weekend hours and work in inclement weather. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver’s license is required to travel between sites. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock or beef industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy. Note: Sponsorships will not be offered for this position. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma plus one year agriculture experience required; additional relevant education may substitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain equipment, machinery, fields, and pastures essential. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet UNL driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with large animals preferred but not required. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe, sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with agriculture, farming, or ranching, including both paid employment and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations). Please specify the number of years of experience you have in this field. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101848": {
      "title": "Finance Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Finance Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Finance Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Finance Specialist Department AVE Business Center-3026 Requisition Number S_260597 Posting Open Date 07/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR’s teaching, research, and extension missions. As a Finance Specialist , with focus on cost accounting and contract administration; you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions. Responsibilities include: Serving as a primary resource for service center and contract administration across IANR , providing strategic guidance and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures. Partnering with departments to develop, manage, and improve service center operations and contractual agreements, promoting effective business practices and sound financial stewardship. Working with faculty and staff to forecast expenses and calculate appropriate service rates based on anticipated activity. Regularly review budget to actual amounts to determine if established rates need to be adjusted. Managing an assigned portfolio, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources including but not limited to state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts. Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions. We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service. This position is located on UNL’s East Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on campus. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs. Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus (4) years of related experience in financial management, accounting, grant administration, or related field. Equivalent combinations of education and experience will be considered. Experience working with SAP or another large integrated financial system. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite or similar software, including Excel for data analysis and reporting. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information in compliance with applicable laws, regulations, and university policies. Strong communication skills and the ability to build positive, collaborative relationships with a variety of stakeholders. Excellent organizational skills with the ability to prioritize work, manage multiple deadlines, and adapt in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred but not required: Experience with grant, project, or cost accounting. Experience providing consultative support, training, or mentoring. Experience in a higher education environment. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $51,961/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jodi Mackin jmackin1@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have any experience with SAP or another fully integrated electronic human resources, financial management or payroll system? If yes, please describe. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail your proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (or similar software). (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
