    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101538": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Chick-fil-A Manager Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Chick-fil-A Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Chick-fil-A Manager Department Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 Requisition Number S_260609 Posting Open Date 07/30/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/12/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Chick-fil-A Manager is responsible for overseeing the daily operations and long-term strategic management of the Chick-fil-A restaurant located in the Nebraska City Union, ensuring operational excellence, exceptional customer service, and achievement of business objectives. The Chick-fil-A Manager will: Demonstrate a commitment to exceptional leadership and customer service Foster and maintain a safe, welcoming environment for customers and team members Exercise independent judgment and discretion in managing the overall operations of the retail location Recruit, hire, train, supervise, and develop team members Ensure all staff meet the operational, service, and brand standards of Chick-fil-A and University Dining Maintain high levels of customer satisfaction and product quality Monitor and manage financial performance, including reviewing sales trends and implementing strategies to achieve business goals Forecast inventory needs and order products and supplies to support efficient operations Ensure compliance with safety, security, and operational policies and procedures within the store Uphold the brand standards for branded restaurant concepts it oversees Schedule varies and includes evenings, late nights, and weekend shifts. At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s or equivalent education/experience. Food-related, business, or hotel/restaurant management field. Four years of food service experience with demonstrated career progression, showing increased leadership and responsibility. Experience managing a cash-handling operation necessary. Must exhibit a firm knowledge of excellent food service management practices to include food production, service styles, team building, hiring, staff development, and training. Food Handler’s permit or ability to obtain by passing the Safety and Sanitation test required. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in relevant food/dietetic/hospitality or business field. Knowledge of cost controls, inventory controls and food safety/sanitation programs necessary. Knowledge of personal computers, word processing, spreadsheets, e-mail and internet necessary. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $60,821/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jeremy Richter jrichter12@unl.edu 4024728164 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Evenings, late nights, and weekend shifts. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
