    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101359": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Supervisor, Electrical Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Supervisor, Electrical Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Supervisor, Electrical Department UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 Requisition Number S_260566 Posting Open Date 07/22/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/12/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. We invest in our employees: Vacation, sick, and holiday pay. Medical, dental, and vision insurance. No-cost life insurance. Employee Assistance Program. Parental leave Retirement plans. Tuition assistance for employees and dependents. Exclusive employee discounts. Professional development through training and education. And many more!! As the Supervisor, Electrical, you will: Implement operational priorities established by leadership, and communicate work status, resource needs, escalate issues, and provide reports and updates when applicable. Monitor work activity, service trends, and operational performance metrics, and recommend improvements to electrical services, workflow efficiency, and service delivery. Coordinate electrical installations, inspections, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance activities, and related work assignments across assigned staff and projects. Review estimates, project information, and work plans for accuracy, timeliness, and alignment with assigned priorities. Assign work, monitor staffing coverage, and adjust daily work assignments to support service needs, project schedules, and operational priorities. Track service work, project activity, and assigned tasks to help ensure completion in alignment with scope, schedule, budget, quality, and service expectations. Coordinate with campus departments and stakeholders to ensure electrical activities align with operational needs, project schedules, and institutional priorities. Oversee campus electrical work, such as low voltage, fire alarm, card access, service work, and medium voltage utility-related activities, and ensure work is completed safely, efficiently, and in accordance with applicable codes and standards. Participate in facilities condition assessments and provide input on electrical system needs, deficiencies, and priorities. Identify operational needs and recommend improvements to procedures, equipment, technologies, and contracted services to enhance reliability, safety, and service quality. Support and monitor compliance with safety, environmental, health, accessibility, electrical code, and other applicable standards and reinforce a culture of safety and accountability. Assist with contract coordination, vendor communication, and review of contractor performance to help ensure performance aligns with specifications, budgets, and institutional standards. Maintain collaborative relationships with campus stakeholders, communicate work priorities and project status, manage service expectations, and share feedback with leadership to support continuous improvement. Promote and reinforce a people-centered culture that emphasizes safety, continuous learning, collaboration, customer service, community, and operational excellence. Provide leadership and oversight of staff performance, such as setting goals, communicating expectations, delivering coaching and training, conducting evaluations, documenting performance, and recommending salary adjustments. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/. Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree, technical training, or equivalent experience in electrical systems, electrical technology, construction, maintenance, power distribution, controls, fire alarm systems, access control systems, building systems, or other related field of study. 2+ years of experience coordinating installations, troubleshooting, repairs, inspections, or maintenance activities in electrical operations, construction, maintenance, utilities, or related facilities operations. 2+ years of experience supervising, leading, assigning, or monitoring the work of staff, crews, contractors, or project teams. Knowledge of electrical systems, power distribution, low voltage, fire alarm, access control, and related operations. Knowledge of applicable codes, safety, and regulatory requirements related to electrical operations. Ability to interpret work orders, estimates, blueprints, specifications, technical information, and other electrical documentation. Ability to assign, coordinate, and monitor daily work activities to support service needs, project schedules, and operational priorities. Skilled in identifying operational issues and recommending practical solutions to support safe, reliable, and efficient service delivery. Supervisory skills that support effective oversight, workflow coordination, accountability, engagement, and continuous improvement. Strong analytical thinking and reasoning skills. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively with campus stakeholders, contractors, and operational partners. Excellent organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and respond effectively to changing operational needs. Able to lift 50 lbs. Able to work from a ladder and/or aerial equipment. Available by cell phone to assist with campus emergencies. Available for regular rotations on the weekend and after-hours on-call schedule. State of Nebraska Journeyman Electrical License Must have a valid driver’s license and eligible to drive on University business. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in electrical technology, construction management, industrial technology, facilities management, engineering technology, or other related field of study, or equivalent experience. Experience overseeing low voltage, fire alarm, card access, service work, and medium voltage utility-related activities. Experience coordinating contractors, vendors, stakeholders, and multiple work priorities in support of operations. Experience reviewing estimates, work plans, service requests, and project documentation. Experience supporting compliance with applicable safety standards, electrical codes, and operational policies. Experience using technology and systems for tracking, reporting, scheduling, communication, and operational efficiency. Experience working in a higher education or similarly complex institutional environment. Proficient utilizing work order systems, work tracking, project coordination, and preparing documentation. Knowledge of University operational processes, budgeting practices, and/or institutional policies. Project Management Professional ( PMP ) certification State of Nebraska Contractors License Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Salary commensurate upon experience How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact uopeopleops@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an associate’s degree, technical training, or equivalent experience in electrical systems, electrical technology, construction, maintenance, power distribution, controls, fire alarm systems, access control systems, building systems, or other related field of study? Yes No * Do you have 2+ years of experience coordinating installations, troubleshooting, repairs, inspections, or maintenance activities in electrical operations, construction, maintenance, utilities, or related facilities operations? Yes No * Do you have 2+ years of experience supervising, leading, assigning, or monitoring the work of staff, crews, contractors, or project teams? Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101903": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Engineering and Technology Education Lead Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Engineering and Technology Education Lead Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job.” You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Engineering and Technology Education Lead Department J S Raikes School of Comp Sci & Mgmt-1313 Requisition Number S_260542 Posting Open Date 07/15/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Raikes School Engineering and Technology Education Lead collaborates with Design Studio staff and Capstone Project Sponsor technical contacts to assess and define hardware, software, and data needs for capstone projects. This role is responsible for establishing initial technical requirements and providing ongoing support for projects throughout each project’s lifecycle. Key responsibilities include supporting the onboarding of annual capstone projects; serving as a technical advisor and resource for student teams in partnership with other Design Studio staff; procuring and managing IT equipment inventory; manage software-as-a-service (SaaS) usage and expenditures; and coordinating and executing the technical components of annual Design Studio and Raikes School events. In addition to supporting the Raikes School Design Studio capstone program, the Engineering and Technology Education Lead provides technical support across the Raikes School. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, administering cloud-based services, source control systems, and collaboration platforms. This position serves as the primary administrator of the Raikes School website and acts as the technical liaison between the Raikes School and University ITS and audio-visual teams. For more information on the Design Studio, please visit https://raikes.unl.edu/design-studio/. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in computer science, computer engineering, software engineering, or related technical field and one (1) year of experience in IT services management, or equivalent experience. Demonstrated attention to detail and organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently and manage/prioritize tasks. Evidence of excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to network and build relationships with community and institutional partners. Familiar with modern software development tools and methodologies. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with students or mentoring. Experience working in higher education. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $70,000/year minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job.” You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Katelyn Rife, SHRM -CP HR Specialist – Lead katelyn.rife@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102118": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260716 Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef, sheep, and swine industries. As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will: Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area. Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle. Maintain machinery and fences, Assist with pasture management Assist with the collection of research data. Irregular hours and work in inclement weather is required. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria is required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about UNL benefits and your total compensation at: https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma plus one year experience with the care and management of cattle; equivalent education/experience considered. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Ability to maintain equipment, machinery, fields and pastures essential. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet university driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience working with livestock, including both paid employment and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations).  Make sure to include the number of years of experience. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
