    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99864": {
      "title": "Solidworks Drafting Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Solidworks Drafting Coordinator Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Solidworks Drafting Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Solidworks Drafting Coordinator Department Midwest Roadside Safety Facility-1070 Requisition Number S_260227 Posting Open Date 03/19/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 04/20/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work This position will be responsible for ensuring technical drawings are completed accurately using the 3D computer-aided drafting program, SOLIDWORKS . The individual will complete and coordinate engineering drawings including layouts, parts details, construction or fabrication plans, and Bill of Materials (BOM’s). This employee will review and ensure all drawings completed by student employees are accurate and meet quality requirements. They will also coordinate the modification of existing designs/drawings and other documentation based on feedback and collaboration with engineering team, faculty, and technical personnel. The individual will maintain a priority list and calendar to ensure all deadlines and key dates are met. This individual will be trained to assist with maintaining and completing backup of the server; troubleshooting computer and server problems; upgrade software programs; purchasing computer equipment, and answer computer related questions. In addition, the individual will be trained to perform crash test video processing and analysis. This individual will follow a developed training procedure when training all new staff/students in video analysis, departmental use of the primary design tool SOLIDWORKS and AutoCAD. The individual will assist the Quality Manager in the management of departmental accreditation. These duties will include, but not be limited to, maintaining files, reviewing work procedures, investigating errors, recommending corrective actions, and documenting processes. This individual must maintain a safe and clean work environment by complying with procedures, rules and regulations, and other duties as assigned. As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in Computer-aided drafting or equivalent or equivalent education/experience. One year of experience with detailed drawings for use in fabrication/construction. Knowledge of computer operating systems and Microsoft software applications; including MS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint, and MS Outlook. Excellent communication and math skills. Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate may have a Bachelor’s degree in Computer-aided drafting or a closely related field. Experience assisting with workplace accreditation or assisting with computer/server systems maintenance. Experience in managing staff and/or projects. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $25.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Karla A Lechtenberg, kpolivka@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with detailed drawings for use in fabrication/construction, including years of experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your knowledge of the following computer operating systems and Microsoft software applications: MS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint, and MS Outlook. (Open Ended Question) * Please detail both your communication and math skills. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
