    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101698": {
      "title": "Director of Memorial Stadium Complex",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Director of Memorial Stadium Complex Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Memorial Stadium Complex Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Director of Memorial Stadium Complex Department Athletics-0850 Requisition Number S_260640 Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/17/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Provide leadership and oversight for the daily operations, maintenance, and event readiness of Memorial Stadium, Hawks Championship Center, Osborne Legacy Complex, and other assigned facilities. This position is responsible for ensuring facilities are maintained to the highest standards while supporting the operational needs of Nebraska Athletics, student-athletes, coaches, staff, and guests. The Director serves as the primary facilities lead for the assigned complex, providing leadership for facility operations, maintenance planning, event coordination, staff supervision, and project management. This position participates in an on-call rotation for facility-related emergencies and works evenings, weekends, and holidays as required to support athletic competitions and special events. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Facility Management, Construction Management, Engineering, Business Administration, Sports Management, or a related field and 3 years’ progressive experience in facility operations, maintenance management, or venue management. Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Strong organizational, communication, project management, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and respond to facility emergencies. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience in NCAA Division I Athletics or large public assembly facilities. Experience managing maintenance projects, contractors, and vendor relationships. Knowledge of computerized maintenance management systems ( CMMS ), such as FMX . Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Negotiable How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact John Kelly jkelly45@huskers.com Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
