      "title": "Assistant Coach",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Coach - Women&#39;s Tennis Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Coach - Women's Tennis Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant Coach - Women's Tennis Department Athletics-0850 Requisition Number S_260679 Posting Open Date 08/19/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/27/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Assist Head coach in all aspects of running a Division I Women’s Tennis program. Position requires working irregular hours. Compliance with all institutional, conference, and NCAA rules. Attendance at all monthly compliance rules education meetings. Collaboration with all support areas who serve support program to ensure positive student-athlete experience. Represent self, team, and institution as a positive role- model and ambassador at all times. Engagement with and event planning for letterwinner alumni. Promote individual student-athlete and team achievements on social media. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent education/experience, plus two years’ coaching or competitive experience required. Strong technical/tennis instruction skills required. Excellent leadership and communication skills essential. Ability to understand and demonstrate a commitment to NCAA , Big Ten, and University regulations necessary. Preferred Qualifications Prefer competitive tournament experience in collegiate and/or professional levels. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Salary commensurate with experience How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact German Dalmagro GDALMAGRO@HUSKERS. COM 402-472-6473 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy 