    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101991": {
      "title": "Export Control Coordinator I, II, or III",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Export Control Coordinator I, II, or III Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Export Control Coordinator I, II, or III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Export Control Coordinator I, II, or III Department Rsch Compliance, Integrity, Security-1315 Requisition Number S_260688 Posting Open Date 08/21/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/04/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Office of Research and Innovation at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) is committed to promoting a culture and environment for success in research, scholarship, creative endeavors, and economic development. Conducting novel and impactful research that generates new knowledge, solves real-world problems, and enhances lives is among the most fundamental purposes of the institution. UNL Research and Innovation has an opportunity for qualified candidates to apply for an Export Control Coordinator position within the Office of Research Compliance, Integrity, and Security at one of three levels: Coordinator I, II, or III . The Export Control Coordinator performs functions related to the oversight, guidance and direction of the UNL Export Control Program, processes, and policies. The primary focus of this position is applying policies and regulations to provide expert advice and training to university administrators and employees on matters relating to Export Control and preventing non-compliance with organizational policies and procedures relating to export controlled research. In addition to the above responsibilities, the Export Control Coordinator II and III are responsible for other duties specific to training, creation of TCPs and interaction with the National Strategic Research Institute ( NSRI .) This position will involve/require access to EAR / ITAR related information, materials, or equipment and may require a license approval from the U.S. government. This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite policy. About Us: At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Export Control Coordinator I: Bachelor’s degree plus 1 year of relevant experience at a research university or a clinical or regulatory environment; equivalent education/experience considered. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Strong decision-making, planning, and organizational skills. Solid presentation, negotiation, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and meeting management skills. Understanding of policy and procedure interpretation and implementation. Demonstrated ability to work in a complex multi-tasking environment. Export Control Coordinator II: Bachelor’s degree plus 2 years of relevant experience at a research university or a clinical or regulatory environment; equivalent education/experience considered. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills. Strong decision-making, planning, and organizational skills. Solid presentation, negotiation, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and meeting management skills. Prior experience with policy and procedure interpretation and implementation. Demonstrated ability to work in a complex multi-tasking environment. Export Control Coordinator III : Bachelor’s degree plus 4 years of relevant experience at a research university or a clinical or regulatory environment; equivalent education/experience considered. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills. Strong decision-making skills, planning, and organizational skills. Solid presentation, negotiation, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and meeting management skills. Prior experience with policy and procedure interpretation and implementation. Demonstrated ability to work in a complex multi-tasking environment. Preferred Qualifications Export Control Coordinator I: Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field CITI Trained ECoP ( EAR / ITAR ) Certification Export Control Coordinator II: Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field 4 years of relevant experience at a research university or a clinical or regulatory environment CITI Trained ECoP ( EAR / ITAR ) Certification Export Control Coordinator III : Master’s degree in a STEM field 6 years of relevant experience at a research university or a clinical or regulatory environment CITI Trained ECoP ( EAR / ITAR ) Certification Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Coor I: $50K min; Corr II: $60K min; Coor III: $70K min How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Ember Welsch, Human Resources Specialist Lead Office of Research and Innovation ewelsch2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102190": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: 1. A letter of interest. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Eric Berger, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902, or send an email to lawappointments@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Department College of Law-0899 Requisition Number F_260085 Posting Open Date 09/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The University of Nebraska College of Law invites applications for entry-level and lateral candidates for multiple tenure-track or tenured faculty positions, depending on the candidate’s experience. The primary course needs are First-Year Property and Federal Income Tax. Other course needs include Torts, Corporate Tax, Partnership Tax, Tax-related seminar, Professional Responsibility, Privacy Law, Constitutional Law, Cyber Security Law, Employee Benefits, Real Estate Transactions, Environmental Law, Administrative Law, Natural Resources Law, and Wills and Trusts. General information about the Law College is available at https://law.unl.edu/ . The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications J.D. Degree or equivalent. Superior academic record. Demonstrated interest in relevant substantive areas. The title of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor will be based on the successful candidate’s qualifications. Preferred Qualifications Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: 1. A letter of interest. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Eric Berger, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902, or send an email to lawappointments@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Eric Berger lawappointments@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
