    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101413": {
      "title": "Finance/Grant Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Finance/Grant Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Finance/Grant Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Finance/Grant Specialist Department Big Red Business Center-11350 Requisition Number S_260583 Posting Open Date 07/24/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/10/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Finance/Grant Specialist serves in a customer-facing, consultative role and is responsible for providing finance and grant support in a timely and accurate manner and in compliance with all applicable institutional, UNL , State, and Federal regulations, policies, and guidelines. The Finance/Grant Specialist primarily executes and reviews routine and complex finance and pre-and post-award grant transactions. The Finance/Grant Specialist will work closely with employees within the departments served, as well as functional office staff, providing a high level of customer service and professionalism in all interactions. This position functions under limited supervision and is expected utilize technology to provide professional services. As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus 4 years of related finance or grant management work experience; equivalent education/experience considered. Experience with SAP or large integrated finance system. A willingness and demonstrated ability to learn new hardware and software systems. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality in compliance with rules and regulations, including HIPAA and FERPA guidelines on the disclosure of information. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written and verbal formats. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain positive relationships within and outside of reporting lines. Demonstrated ability to establish priorities and meet deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Experience performing project or cost accounting. Experience conducting training. Experience serving multiple units as part of a service team. Experience performing grant-related tasks at a University of Nebraska institution. Experience with NuGrant or similar grants management system. Knowledge of federal and state laws and guidelines related to business practices. Knowledge of grant terminology and practices. Demonstrated ability to coach and mentor others. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $51,961/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your cover letter, resume, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Katelyn Rife, SHRM -CP HR Specialist – Lead katelyn.rife@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101906": {
      "title": "Research Communications Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Research Communications Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Research Communications Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Research Communications Specialist Department Research Communications-13275 Requisition Number S_260557 Posting Open Date 07/22/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/03/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Research Communications Specialist is an integral part of the team that leads communications and marketing efforts for the Office of Research and Innovation (R&I). The team promotes research, scholarly and creative endeavors at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln and ensures that the university researcher community is aware of the resources, opportunities and support available through R&I. The position is geared toward a strong writer and editor who is able to translate complex information and convey the impact of Nebraska researchers’ work in an engaging and accessible manner. The Research Communications Specialist is responsible for writing and editing content that is used across a variety of platforms, including news releases, websites, reports and newsletters. This position also executes communications and marketing tasks for lectures, conferences, workshops and other events hosted by R&I. Additionally, the specialist regularly updates website content on research.unl.edu. The ideal candidate demonstrates exceptional attention to detail and works well in a collaborative, team-oriented environment. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in journalism, public relations, marketing, communications or related field plus three years of relevant professional communications experience in newsroom, university, agency, public relations/communications, government, or nonprofit environments, or equivalent. Experience in writing and editing news stories and/or other types of content that adhere to journalistic standards for accuracy, clarity and style. Demonstrated professional writing and editing skills Demonstrated knowledge of and experience applying Associated Press (AP) style. Preferred Qualifications Ability to interview subject-matter experts about their research, scholarship and/or creative work and translate that information into engaging stories for the intended audience. Flexibility, adaptability and skills to simultaneously work on multiple projects. Experience writing about complex topics, especially those related to research, scholarship and/or creative endeavors for lay audiences. Professional communications experience in a university or government setting. Experience using a content management system, such as WordPress, Drupal or similar. Experience using Adobe Creative Suite. Experience in promoting events and/or outreach activities for an organization. Experience using website analytics to gather information and inform content strategy. Photography and/or videography skills Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $54,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Ember Welsch, Human Resources Specialist Lead Office of Research and Innovation ewelsch2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102121": {
      "title": "Proposal Development Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Proposal Development Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Proposal Development Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Nebraska Working Title Proposal Development Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator Department Research Development-13276 Requisition Number S_260718 Posting Open Date 09/01/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/14/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Office of Research and Innovation (R&I) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) is committed to promoting a culture and environment for success in research, scholarship, creative endeavors, and economic development. Conducting novel and impactful research that generates new knowledge, solves real-world problems, and enhances lives is among the most fundamental purposes of the institution. The Office of Proposal Development seeks to hire a Proposal Development professional at one of three levels: Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator. This position joins a team of research development professionals to provide comprehensive proposal development assistance to UNL faculty, staff, and administrators. The primary responsibilities of the proposal development specialist and coordinator are to edit single investigator and small group grant proposals and provide editorial support for colleagues developing large, complex proposals. In addition, the proposal development coordinator also manages the development of large-scale, collaborative proposals. The primary responsibilities of the senior proposal development coordinator are coaching faculty about best practices for proposal writing; preparing faculty to network with program officers; co-authoring, reviewing, and refining individual investigator and small group grant applications; and managing the development of large-scale, collaborative proposals. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/. Minimum Required Qualifications Proposal Development Specialist: Bachelor’s degree in English, journalism, communications, or a relevant scientific discipline. Excellent writing, editing, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated flexibility, adaptability, and ability to manage multiple projects. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite. Proposal Development Coordinator: Bachelor’s degree in English, journalism, communications, or a relevant scientific discipline plus three years of demonstrated experience writing and/or editing grant proposals in the public or private sector. Excellent writing, editing, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated flexibility, adaptability, and ability to simultaneously manage multiple projects. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite. Demonstrated ability to problem solve and independently make decisions in a deadline-driven environment. Senior Proposal Development Coordinator: Master’s degree in English, journalism, communications, or a relevant scientific discipline plus five years of demonstrated experience writing and/or editing grant proposals in the public or private sector. Demonstrated ability to provide comprehensive proposal development assistance for large-scale interdisciplinary, multi-institutional projects. Excellent writing, editing, and interpersonal communication skills. Exceptional organizational skills and attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to quickly become familiar with complex subject matter in a wide variety of academic disciplines. Demonstrated flexibility, adaptability, and ability to simultaneously manage multiple projects. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite Demonstrated ability to problem solve and independently make decisions in a deadline-driven environment. Knowledge and understanding of national research priorities and funding agencies. Experience managing complex teams of professionals from diverse backgrounds in a highly competitive environment. Preferred Qualifications Proposal Development Specialist: Demonstrated experience writing and/or editing grant proposals in the public or private sector. Proposal Development Coordinator: Master’s degree preferred. Professional experience in a university setting. Senior Proposal Development Coordinator: Professional experience in a university setting. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary Negotiable based on qualifications and experience How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Ember Welsch, Human Resources Coordinator Lead Office of Research & Economic Development ewelsch2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Occasional nights & weekends Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100064": {
      "title": "Outreach and Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Outreach and Engagement Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Outreach and Engagement Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your list of references, cover letter and resume/CV as three separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Outreach and Engagement Specialist Department School of Natural Resources-0844 Requisition Number S_260269 Posting Open Date 04/07/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 05/18/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work For over 30 years, the High Plains Regional Climate Center ( HPRCC ) has been providing the public with access to the most up-to-date climate data and information available. We provide a variety of resources, including near real-time and historical climate data, national and regional climate data maps, agricultural climate products, and regional climate summaries. As an Outreach and Engagement Specialist, you will: Analyze, interpret, and retrieve climate data to produce educational materials for the public on the HPRCC website, including informational material on HPRCC products, product updates, and instructional guides. Work independently to produce summaries or recaps of notable weather and climate events within the High Plains region. Use MS Office programs, Adobe InDesign, and ArcGIS products to create educational materials and custom maps based on user and stakeholder needs. Serve as the point of contact for outreach and engagement activities, coordinating and leading in-person and virtual public presentations, meetings, workshops, conferences, and joint outreach events. Assist HPRCC staff with ongoing projects and daily activities, including QA/QC of climate databases, feedback on product and tool development, and external work requests. Track and evaluate the success of the education and outreach programs. In the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Field Training Specialist. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree with relevant course work in weather and climate science, plus one year of experience working with weather and climate data and information, including analysis and interpretation. Demonstrated ability in outreach and engagement activities. Effective written and oral communication skills, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks. Experience with MS Office programs. Valid driver’s license with ability to meet university driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred, but not required: Master’s degree Experience coordinating projects, events, or outreach activities. Knowledge of the climate in the High Plains; meteorology/climatology; and understanding of regional climatology. Experience with Adobe InDesign and ArcGIS products. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $56,400/year minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your list of references, cover letter and resume/CV as three separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Nicolas Bretta at nbretta2@unl.edu or 402-472-6238 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101727": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Sheep Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Sheep Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Sheep Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) Department USMARC-0937 Requisition Number S_260644 Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/19/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center ( USMARC ) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. As a Sheep Ranch Hand, you will: Be responsible for care of livestock to include feeding, observation, and treatment of sheep population. Service and maintain equipment and buildings in the sheep facilities. Maintain the sanitation of sheep facilities. Irregular hours and work in inclement weather is required. Ability to travel between locations onsite is required.  In the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.  In the livestock industry, this position may be referred to as a herdsman or shepherd. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent plus one year of ranch/farm experience required. Additional relevant education may substitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Precision, accuracy and attention to detail necessary. Knowledge of farm machinery and equipment operation necessary. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet University driving requirements. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with sheep and other livestock preferred but not required. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.55/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sheila Trampe sheila.trampe@usda.gov Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Clay Center, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your experience with agriculture, farming, or ranching, including both paid employment and unpaid experience (e.g., work on family operations). Please specify the number of years of experience you have in this field. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
