    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101612": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, Student Culture and Community",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Program Coordinator, Student Culture and Community Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Program Coordinator, Student Culture and Community Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Program Coordinator, Student Culture and Community Department Student Culture & Community-11400 Requisition Number S_260563 Posting Open Date 08/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/20/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work We’re looking for someone to join our team to support a dynamic student community. The Program Coordinator advances student belonging and holistic success by coordinating programs, services, and engagement opportunities that support all students at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln. This position helps cultivate welcoming spaces and campus-wide connections where students can access resources, build supportive relationships, and participate in meaningful community experiences. Through intentional programming, partnership development, and student-centered engagement, the Program Coordinator strengthens inclusive excellence and contributes to a campus climate where all students can thrive. The Program Coordinator will: Support the development of a campus-wide culture of belonging. Facilitate and support programming efforts, including affinity-based communities, dialogue spaces, and mobile engagement opportunities that promote identity exploration, connection, and belonging. Coordinate and implement embedded gender and sexuality engagement initiatives across campus including; student spaces, and campus environments to increase access, visibility, and impact. Serve as a key partner with Residence Life and campus collaborators, supporting the integration of identity-affirming practices within daily student environments. Assist with training initiatives for student-facing staff (e.g., Resident Assistants, desk staff, and student leaders). Contribute to outreach and engagement strategies that expand participation and reduce barriers to access for students across varying stages of identity development. Assist in building and maintaining internal and external partnerships that enhance student engagement, community connection, and holistic support. About Us: The Office of Student Culture & Community fosters dynamic and supportive environments, provides empowering experiences, and supports all students to strengthen a sense of belonging and holistic success. We cultivate spaces, programs, and partnerships where all Huskers can engage genuinely, meaningfully, and thrive in community. We advance student success by connecting individuals to resources that address basic needs, support academic and personal development, and build leadership capacity. We empower students not only to navigate campus life but also to shape it. At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Ample paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Employee & dependent scholarship program to pursue higher education Generous retirement plans with university match Learn more about working for UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s or equivalent education/experience One year of experience in higher education, student life, cultural engagement, student support services, or related field. Experience developing, implementing, and assessing student-centered programs or initiatives. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships with students, student organizations, campus partners, alumni, and community stakeholders. Previous experience coordinating programs, events, workshops, and community-building opportunities. Basic knowledge of student development, identity-based support, campus engagement, or community-building practices. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Sociology, Educational Psychology/Psychology, Leadership, Program Management/Administration or related field. Experience working with student organizations, peer leaders, or student-led initiatives. Experience supporting programs or services related to belonging, identity development, or student community-building. Experience working through collaborative or embedded service models across campus environments. Experience generating external funding sources (fundraising, grants, etc.). Experience developing and implementing workshops, programs, and services related to gender and sexuality. Previous experience developing and implementing comprehensive communication and outreach plans. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Strong organization, time management, and attention to detail. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $48,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Kenji Madison kmadison2@unl.edu 402.472-1877 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Some evenings and weekends Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101994": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Registrar Information Systems Developer Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Registrar Information Systems Developer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Registrar Information Systems Developer Department Office of the University Registrar-0961 Requisition Number S_260656 Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Create new reports, electronic forms, workflows, and other electronic processes using the suite of development tools within the student information system. Write XSL expressions within system tools to create electronic documents and communications. Deliver content to the student information system’s end-users in easy to consume formats. Use SQL , WebFOCUS coding and other system tools to write queries against the student information system. Create system interfaces between the Student Information System and other subsidiary systems. Create data branching logic to create datasets that can be consumed by reporting and data analysis tools. Determine means to meet end-users’ reporting and analysis needs throughout the university. Act as a resource to UNL system users and functional administrators, provide regular updates, and answer questions. Possess and maintain a practical knowledge of university policies and processes. Communicate effectively with individuals of varying system expertise and business needs. Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. As an EO/AA employer, qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See: http://www.unl.edu/equity/notice-nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Business Analytics, Computer Science, Management of Information Systems, or related field and 1 year of employment experience with data science, business analytics, or information systems; Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Knowledge of information systems Ability to conduct database queries and report writing. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Two or more years of full-time, applicable employment experience desirable. Experience in higher education setting. Knowledge of how university work is accomplished helpful. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $65,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Sandy Airan, sairan2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101059": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Early Childhood Data Collector (Part-Time: On-Call) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Early Childhood Data Collector (Part-Time: On-Call) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Early Childhood Data Collector (Part-Time: On-Call) Department NE Ctr Research on Youth, Fam & School-4425 Requisition Number S_260503 Posting Open Date 07/06/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 07/16/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Part-time, on-call data collectors needed to help fulfill many research functions in the Nebraska Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families and Schools at the University of Nebraska – Lincoln. Responsibilities Include: Field-based data collection and professional representation Travel to schools across Lincoln and rural areas of Nebraska,. Serve as the face of the research team in the field, coordinating schedules, conducting assessments, and upholding confidentiality and professional standards Administering assessments and maintaining reliability Conduct questionnaires with parents and administer standardized assessments to young children (ages 3–6) Complete training to achieve and maintain reliability on all assessment measures Supporting logistics and data management Assist with scheduling assessments, scoring, checking data, and coordinating with other data collectors Contribute to data management tasks and ensure accurate documentation The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Associate’s degree with some coursework in psychology, education, child development or related field and at least six months experience working with young children (ages 3-6 years); Additional relevant experience may substitute for education on a year-for-year basis. Experience with Microsoft Office, including Word and Excel, and video-recording equipment. Flexible availability during weekdays (7am-8pm) and/or weekends. Must be available to work a minimum of 10 hours up to 40 hours during these times. Detail-oriented, highly organized, able to work independently with minimal supervision. Dependable transportation. Familiarity with basic technology (e.g., iPad, video-recording equipment). Valid driver’s license and approved to drive on University business. Preferred Qualifications A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in psychology, education, child development or related field. One year of research experience, including assessment administration, classroom observations, scoring, or data entry. Preschool classroom experience. Knowledge of development in young children and child assessments. Knowledge of working with families. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $18.00/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Tammi Hechtner thechtner2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Office/Service Job Type Part-Time Temporary Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Rate your ability (beginner, intermediate, advanced) using the following Microsoft office products:  Outlook for email and calendaring, Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101877": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Facility Services Manager Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Facility Services Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of professional references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Facility Services Manager Department Lied Center for Performing Arts-0854 Requisition Number S_250585 Posting Open Date 07/24/2025 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/11/2025 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Facility Services Manager oversees all care, maintenance and project needs for the Lied Center for Performing Arts, including physical plant and its operating systems, interior furnishings and fixtures. Directs all aspects of building maintenance and housekeeping, conversion and engineering tasks related to the operation of the Lied Center. Oversees the supervision of the building maintenance staff and manages the custodial staff. Conducts yearly staff performance evaluations and ensures adherence to building policy and procedures. Plans and budgets for renovation projects, building upkeep, repairs, furnishing replacements and fire, life and safety projects. Creates the scope of work required for projects to be worked in-house, or seeks out contractors and bids and works with UNL FMP code officials on acquiring permits, scheduling work, quality control, ensuring regulatory and code compliance and ensuring deadlines are met and work is performed in a professional manner. Prioritizes all building events with repairs and project needs. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent plus four years of experience with building construction and remodel, including two years of preventive maintenance work on mechanical, electrical, and HVAC systems. Experience in training, motivating, and supervising staff. Custodial experience. Customer service experience. Working knowledge of electrical systems, steam systems, HVAC /Refrigeration, and plumbing repair. Familiarity with and skilled in the use of an extensive variety of both hand and power tools. Familiarity with basic safety procedures and OSHA Guidelines. Knowledge of the safe and effective use of cleaning chemicals and operation of tools and equipment used in custodial operations. Basic computer and email skills. Ability to develop, maintain, and follow a budget. Experience must demonstrate attention to detail and ability to follow through on projects. Must have a valid driver’s license and meet University driver eligibility requirements. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree plus four or more years of experience performing comparable duties in a similar venue. Experience that demonstrates welding, plumbing, carpeting, soldering, carpentry, painting, laminating, drywall, and finishing skills. Licensed general contractor. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Yes Physical Required Yes Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $70,000/yr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter and list of professional references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Natalie Stroud nstroud2@unl.edu 402-472-4752 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Evenings & weekends required based on events & building service needs. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
