    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102023": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Digital Marketing Specialist Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Digital Marketing Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information Eeo Statement Working Title Digital Marketing Specialist Department University Television-0912 Requisition Number S_260670 Posting Open Date 08/18/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Digital Marketing Specialist executes Nebraska Public Media’s digital marketing campaigns across paid search, paid social, programmatic advertising, and audience targeting platforms. Reporting to the Marketing & Audience Development Manager, this position implements approved campaign strategies, manages the Google Ad Grant program, builds and monitors paid campaigns, and leads digital promotional execution for assigned initiatives. This role focuses on tactical campaign execution, paid media management, digital advertising operations, performance tracking, and coordination of promotional deliverables to support goals of the Communications & Engagement Department and overall strategic priorities. Nebraska Public Media offers a full spectrum of communications services to the citizens of Nebraska. Some of these services include a statewide noncommercial public television network affiliated with PBS ; statewide noncommercial public radio network affiliated with NPR ; a cutting-edge Digital Media Group; and state-of-the-art audio, video and multimedia production capability delivered via broadcast, satellite, cable, Internet and broadband delivery channels. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two (2) years’ experience building and managing paid search, paid social, or programmatic advertising campaigns. Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis. Experience using digital analytics tools to monitor and evaluate campaign performance. Excellent writing, editing, and data analysis skills. Proficiency with Google Ads and Google Analytics. Knowledge of SEO and retargeting. Strong organizational, planning and time management skills and techniques. Preferred Qualifications Experience managing a Google Ad Grant account. Experience with programmatic advertising platforms such as StackAdapt. Experience in public media or mission-driven organizations. Experience with the Google for Nonprofits program. Knowledge of media industry. Relationship-based service/marketing experience. Proficiency with social media business tools. Familiarity with content management systems, Google Search Console, paid search, and email marketing. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $53,477 minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Humanresources@Nebraskapublicmedia.org Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101431": {
      "title": "FARRP Program Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | FARRP Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FARRP Program Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume and list of references as two separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title FARRP Program Coordinator Department Food Science & Technology-0836 Requisition Number S_260586 Posting Open Date 07/27/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 08/14/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Food Allergy Research and Resource Program ( FARRP ) works to develop and provide the food industry with credible information, expert opinions, tools, and services relating to a broad range of food allergen topics. FARRP takes a comprehensive approach, working and collaborating with research institutions, governmental authorities, consumer groups, and scientific societies around the globe to improve the safety of food products for consumers. As a FARRP Program Coordinator , you will: Lead day-to-day financial operations for FARRP , providing operational and financial support to the co-directors across a complex portfolio of funding sources, projects, program activities, and revenue streams. Serve as a primary financial advisor to the co-directors, conducting critical, time-sensitive financial analyses, identifying trends, and developing recommendations to support strategic and operational decision-making related to budgeting, compliance, and resource allocation. Serve as the primary point of contact for industry stakeholders on all non-scientific matters, managing ongoing relationships, coordinating communications, and facilitating access to program resources. Develop and execute strategic member engagement and communication initiatives that strengthen relationships, support long-term program objectives, and enhance the value of FARRP membership. Lead the planning and execution of the large-scale annual FARRP Board meeting, workshops, and other events by independently managing complex logistics, budgets, vendor relationships, contractual negotiations, and external partners. Lead operational implementation of FARRP outreach initiatives developed by leadership, including in-person events, virtual programming, online courses, publications, and other educational resources. Provide strategic input to support the program’s communication objectives and manage day-to-day operations of the FARRP website and external communication channels. Provide direct supervision and leadership for the administrative support team, focusing on workload coordination, performance management, and professional development. Occasional travel is required for program events. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Admin Associate. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business, public administration, communications, or related field plus five (5) years’ experience in program or operations coordination. Additional years of relevant experience or completed relevant education may substitute for required education/experience on a year-for-year basis . Experience managing multiple budgets and exercising independent judgment. Supervisory experience with responsibility for staff oversight. Preferred Qualifications The following qualifications are preferred, but not required: Experience in research‑intensive or externally funded programs. Experience managing memberships, industry partnerships, or advisory boards. Experience overseeing outreach or educational programs and advising senior leadership on program operations. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $24.04/hr minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume and list of references as two separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Melissa Weiler at Mweiler4@nebraska.edu or 402-473-9604 Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101947": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives (Open to University Staff Only)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives (Open to University Staff Only) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives (Open to University Staff Only) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives (Open to University Staff Only) Department College of Arts & Sciences-0906 Requisition Number S_260676 Posting Open Date 08/20/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 09/04/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives provides oversight of academic advising, new student onboarding, and student success initiatives within the College of Arts and Sciences. Responsibilities include coordinating college participation in new student enrollment and orientation programs; supervising, developing, and assessing professional advising staff; leading advisor training and workload management; supporting college-wide retention, persistence, and graduation initiatives; maintaining a limited advising caseload while providing complex academic guidance; collaborating with academic departments and campus partners to improve student success outcomes; and contributing to assessment, data analysis, and continuous improvement efforts. The role also serves on college and university committees and advances professional development and best practices in academic advising. About Us At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy: Generous paid time off , including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays Comprehensive insurance options , including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education Robust retirement plans with university match Learn more about working at UNL : https://go.unl.edu/aboutus The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/. Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of experience in higher education with evidence of 1:1 student interaction in advising or related areas. Ability to learn and explain extensive university/college requirements, federal law, policies and procedures. Experience using a variety of technology platforms. Must have strong leadership skills and supervisory experience. Must have excellent interpersonal, communication, organization, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively in a team environment essential. Ability to learn extensive requirements, policies, and procedures; Ability to lead projects, build relationships and collaborate across functional units. Preferred Qualifications Background in liberal arts and sciences desirable. 3 years direct academic advising experience helpful. Public speaking skills preferred. Experience helping students explore and pursue career opportunities. Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required No Physical Required No Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) required. Subject to DOT approved pre-employment & random testing for alcohol and controlled substances. No Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary $60,000/yr. minimum How to Apply Click on “Apply for this Job”. You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach your resume, cover letter, and list of references as three (3) separate documents in MS Word or PDF format. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Niveen Dineh, ndineh2@unl.edu Job Category (old) Managerial/Professional Job Type Full-Time Alternate Work Schedule (if other than 8-5) Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date: Appointment End Date Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
